 Surgical Oncology faculty, we recommended a <1>neoadjuvant chemotherapy</1> strategy followed by ***** his surgical prospects. He initiated ***** on 03/06/2022, once his <2>LFTs</2> had sufficiently normalized post-<3>stent</3>, and is now s/p 3 cycles of treatment. The patient's present review of systems was reviewed. He continues to tolerate <4>chemotherapy</4> quite well overall; his last cycle in fact was a/w less <5>hiccups</5>, <6>fatigue</6>, and <7>cold sensitivity</7>/<8>peripheral sensory neuropathy</8> than previously. He reports maintenance of a good appetite, and no <9>abdominal pain</9>, <10>diarrhea</10>, <11>fevers</11> or <12>chills</12>. He is staying active, walking and still playing golf. PAST MEDICAL AND SURGICAL HISTORY <13>Fatty liver disease</13> <14>Chronic rhinitis</14> Current Outpatient Medications Medication Instructions baclofen <15>5 mg</15>, Oral, 2 Times Daily PRN, TAKE 1 TO 2 TABLETS BY MOUTH TWICE DAILY AS NEEDED FOR <16>HICCUPS</16> calcium carbonate/<17>vitamin D3</17> (<18>VITAMIN D-3 ORAL</18>) Oral lidocaine-prilocaine (<19>EMLA</19>) <20>2.5-2.5 % cream</20> Apply cream one hour before port access as needed for <21>pain</21>. loperamide (<22>IMODIUM</22>) <23>2 mg capsule</23> Take two capsules by mouth at the onset of <24>diarrhea</24>, then take one capsule every 2 hours until <25>diarrhea</25>-free for 12 hours. LORazepam (<26>ATIVAN</26>) <27>1 mg</27>, Oral, Every 6 Hours PRN ondansetron (<28>ZOFRAN</28>) <29>8 mg tablet</29> Take 1 tablet three times a day as needed for <30>nausea</30> and <31>vomiting</31>. Start 2 days after last dose of <32>palonosetron</32> (*****) is given. prochlorperazine (<33>COMPAZINE</33>) <34>10 mg</34>, Oral, Every 6 Hours PRN selenium <35>200 mcg tablet</35> Oral, Daily Scheduled
