ner_results: ```plaintext
<1>hepatic lobe</1> measuring up to 8 mm in short axis. <2>Gallbladder</2>: Surgically absent <3>Spleen</3>: Surgically absent <4>Pancreas</4>: Unremarkable. No <5>pancreatic ductal dilatation</5>. Although the pancreas is completely surrounded by centrally necrotic <6>lymphadenopathy</6>, there is no definite mass arising from the pancreas itself. <7>Adrenal Glands</7>: Unremarkable <8>Kidneys</8>: There are a few low-density lesions within the kidneys bilaterally, too small to characterize further by <9>CT</9>. <10>Vasculature</10>: Mild scattered calcific atheromatous disease. <11>GI Tract</11>: Circumferential heterogeneously enhancing mass in the <12>ascending colon</12> measuring approximately 4.3 cm in transverse dimension with suggestion of adjacent surface implants between the <13>hepatic flexure</13> and the <14>right hepatic lobe</14>. <15>Pelvis</15>: Unremarkable <16>Lymphadenopathy</16>: Extensive centrally necrotic lymphadenopathy throughout the abdomen and pelvis including <17>retrocaval</17>, <18>peripancreatic</18>, <19>periaortic</19>, <20>aortocaval</20>, <21>porta hepatis</21>, <22>mesenteric</22>, <23>pericardiophrenic</23>, and <24>external iliac distributions</24>. One of the largest nodes is peripancreatic and measures 3.8 x 1.9cm <25>Ascites</25>: Absent <26>Bones</26>: No suspicious lesions <27>11/01/2012</27>  IMPRESSION:  1. Circumferential heterogeneously enhancing mass in the ascending colon measuring approximately 4.3 cm in transverse dimension.  1. Extensive centrally necrotic lymphadenopathy throughout the abdomen and pelvis. Although the pancreas is completely surrounded by necrotic lymphadenopathy, there is no definite mass arising from the pancreas itself. This appearance is atypical for <28>pancreatic adenocarcinoma</28> and alternate diagnostic considerations such as <29>metastatic colon cancer</29> may be *****.  END OF IMPRESSION:     <30>Ct Chest With Contrast</30>    <31>10/30/2012</31>  <32>CT CHEST</32> ***** *****/*****/***** *****:***** PM  CLINICAL HISTORY: <33>52 yo female</33> with <34>metastatic pancreas ca</34>, baseline prior to starting treatment  COMPARISON: None  TECHNIQUE: Serial <35>1.25 mm axial images</35> through the chest were obtained after 
