 time (<1>CT scans</1> <2>04/08/2020</2>) showed further <3>disease progression</3> in <4>lungs</4>, <5>liver</5>, and <6>lymph nodes</6>. <7>Liver biopsy</7> the following day confirmed <8>adenocarcinoma</8>    After extensive discussions w/Ms. ***** and her family re: her prognosis and the role and potential toxicities a/w <9>systemic therapy</9> esp in light of her challenging social circumstances (including ongoing heavy <10>EtOH consumption</10>), she ultimately initiated <11>chemotherapy</11> with empirically dose-reduced ***** beginning on <12>05/26/2020</12>. Repeat <13>CT scans</13> after <14>4 treatment cycles</14> showed reasonable <15>disease control</15> with only one area of slight growth in the <16>liver</16> (segment 8), but other areas (<17>liver</17>, <18>lung</18>, <19>LNs</19>) stable or slightly decreased in size; furthermore, she appeared to be deriving ***** favorable clinical benefit from treatment. On these bases, she continued with the same ***** regimen, with repeat <20>CT scans</20> after <21>8 cycles</21> showing, again, only slight increase in ***** single <22>hepatic lesion</22>, this time in segment 2. She has since gone on to complete <23>11 cycles of chemotherapy</23> in total, most recently on <24>10/21/2020</24>.    Interval history/review of systems  - Some cumulative treatment-related <25>fatigue</25>  - <26>Abdominal pain</26> fairly well-controlled on stable dose of ***** *****  - <27>Sluggish appetite</27>  - Fairly regular <28>BMs</28>  - Mild non-progressive, non-debilitating <29>peripheral sensory neuropathy</29>  - Splits time between living independently at home and with family  - No <30>SOB</30>, <31>cough</31>, or <32>respiratory symptoms</32>.  - Family indicates she is still <33>smoking</33> and <34>drinking EtOH</34> ***** fair amount each day.      Current Outpatient Medications   Medication Instructions    <35>acetaminophen (TYLENOL)</35> <36>1,000 mg</36>, <37>Oral</37>, <38>Every 8 Hours</38> Scheduled    <39>albuterol</39> <40>90 mcg/actuation</40> <41>metered dose inhaler</41> <42>2 puffs</42>, <43>Inhalation</43>, <44>Every 6 Hours</44> PRN    <45>amLODIPine (NORVASC)</45> <46>10 mg tablet</46> No dose, route, or frequency recorded.    ***** <47>25 mg capsule</47> No dose, route, or frequency recorded.    <48>bisacodyL (DULCOLAX)</48> <49>10 mg</49>, <50>Rectal</50>, <51>Daily</51> PRN    
