Subjective   ***** ***** ***** is a 52 y.o. male who presents for f/u of recurrent grade 1 <1>pancreatic neuroendocrine tumor</1> s/p ***** procedure in 2013 for <2>5 cm nonfunctional tumor</2>. Patient also with underlying <3>hepatitis B</3>.         Oncologic history:    Patient presented with <4>post-prandial abdominal discomfort</4>, <5>early satiety</5> and <6>emesis</6> in May 2012. <7>CT abdomen</7> obtained on 06/25/12 revealed <8>enlarged pancreatic head</8> measuring <9>48.7x44.9x46.6mm</9> along with <10>dilatation of the pancreatic duct</10>. <11>SMA artery</11> was not encased but a <12>portacaval lymph node</12> measuring <13>18.7x5</13>.***** was noted. There was <14>intrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation</14> in the <15>liver</15> and <16>CBD dilatation</16> without any <17>focal liver lesions</17>.     An <18>EUS</18> was done on 07/05/12 and showed a <19>mass involving the head of the pancreas</19> measuring <20>4.5x4</20>.***** which was causing <21>partial obstruction</21> in ***** and abutting the <22>SMV</22> and <23>portal vein</23>. <24>FNA of the pancreatic mass</24> showed <25>grade 2 pancreatic neuroendocrine tumor</25> (<26>ki-67 proliferation index</26> is <27>3%</27>) with <28>IHC stains</28> positive for <29>synaptophysin</29> and <30>CGA</30>. Patient also had an <31>OctreoScan</31> on 07/19/12 which showed <32>extensive radiotracer uptake</32> within the <33>pancreatic head mass</33> but no <34>metastatic sites</34>. <35>Clinically Nonfunctional tumor</35>.    07/11/12  <36>HepB viral DNA</36> <37>1580</37>  <38>Insulin</38>:<39>7</39>  <40>Proinsulin</40> <41>15.2</41>  <42>Glucagon</42> <43><134</43>  <44>Gastrin</44> <45>23</45>  <46>CGA</46> <47>5.6</47>  <48>Panc polypeptide</48> <49>365</49>    <50>CT chest</50> was obtained for staging purposes on 07/25/12 and did not reveal any concerning findings for <51>metastatic disease</51>.     July 2012: s/p <52>pylorus preserving</52> ***** procedure with <53>reconstruction of SMV</53>, <54>cholecystectomy</54> and <55>liver biopsy</55> by Dr. ***** at *****. <56>Pathology</56>(+) <57>5.5cm well-differentiated neuroendocrine tumor</57>, <58>grade 1</58> (<59>ki-67%</59> <60><2%</60>) with <61>lymphovascular</61> and <62>perineural invasion</62>. May <63>42 lymph nodes</63> were involved with <64>metastatic disease</64>. The <65>liver biopsy</65> showed <66>chronic hepatitis B</66>, <67>fibrosis grade 0</67> and <68>multifocal</68> ***** <69>hepatocellular necrosis</69>.     The post-operative course was complicated 
``` 
