Imaging:    10/05/2015  <1>Pet</1> *****-***** <2>Wb</2> (*****)  COMPARISON: None  FINDINGS:  HEAD/NECK: Physiologic <3>somatostatin receptor uptake</3> is noted in the <4>pituitary gland</4>.  No evidence of <5>receptor positive metastasis</5>.   CHEST: <6>Lungs</6> are clear.  No foci of <7>receptor positive metastatic disease</7>.    ABDOMEN/PELVIS: ***** <8>tracer uptake</8> is identified within an enlarged <9>retroperitoneal lymph node</9> (SUV max <10>82.4</10>) at the level of the <11>pancreatic head</11>. There are <12>2 additional foci of increased tracer uptake</12> without definite <13>MRI</13> correlate within the nearby <14>retroperitoneum</14> possibly representing sites of <15>metastatic disease</15>. There are <16>multiple foci of increased tracer uptake</16> primarily within the <17>right hepatic lobe</17>.  MUSCULOSKELETAL:   No foci of <18>receptor positive osseous metastatic disease</18>.     IMPRESSION: 1. <19>Retroperitoneal adenopathy</19> including a dominant enlarged <20>lymph node</20> at the level of <21>pancreatic head</21> along with <22>multiple foci of increased uptake</22> within the <23>liver</23> is compatible with <24>metastatic disease</24>.  This study was reviewed by <25>Dr.</25> ***** *****, <26>nuclear medicine</26> 10/05/2015 Mr ***** ***** ***** Without 
``` 
