E. <1>MESENTERY</1>, <2>LYMPH NODE</2>, <3>BIOPSY</3> -- ONE <4>LYMPH NODE</4> POSITIVE FOR <5>CARCINOMA</5> (October 02) COMMENT: Histologic sections of the <6>pancreatic mass</6> in ***** ***** show a well-differentiated <7>ductal adenocarcinoma</7> with three positive <8>lymph nodes</8> (Stage <9>pT3 N1</9>). Additional details are provided in the summary table below. <10>PANCREAS CARCINOMA SUMMARY</10> Site <11>Head of pancreas</11> Specimen Type ***** <12>pancreaticoduodenectomy</12> Tumor Type <13>Ductal adenocarcinoma</13> Size: 3.5 x 3.5 x 3.0 cm Grade <14>Well-differentiated</14> <15>Common Bile Duct Margin</15> Negative <16>Distal Pancreatic Margin</16> Negative <17>Posterior Margin</17> Negative <18>Retroperitoneal/Uncinate Process Margin</18> Negative <19>Lymphovascular Invasion</19> Not identified <20>Lymph Node Status</20> Three <21>lymph nodes</21>, positive for <22>carcinoma</22> (December 25) Largest Metastatic Focus 0.5 cm <23>Extracapsular Extension</23> Not present <24>Distant Metastasis</24> Not provided <25>TNM (AJCC, 7th Edition) pT3</25> ***** His postoperative course was notable for slow bowel recovery requiring a period of <26>TPN</26> and a <27>pancreaticojejunal leak</27>, managed conservatively with <28>percutaneous drainage</28> and <29>antibiotic coverage</29>. He was ultimately discharged from the hospital on 06/25/2015 and was able to initiate <30>adjuvant chemotherapy</30> with the combination of <31>gemcitabine</31> plus *****-<32>paclitaxel</32> beginning in mid-July. He completed 3 full cycles on a three-week-on, one-week-off dosing schedule, but beginning cycle #4 the *****-<33>paclitaxel</33> was d/c'ed 2o to cumulative <34>peripheral sensory neuropathy</34>. On <35>gemcitabine</35> alone his ***** is significantly improved. He is scheduled to start cycle #5 this upcoming week. The patient's present review of systems was reviewed and notable for the following: - Persistent but gradually resolving <36>peripheral sensory neuropathy</36>, somewhat affecting fine motor tasks - Somewhat <37>fatigued</37>, although still working (mostly from home) - Complete <38>alopecia</38> - Uses <39>oxycodone</39> sparingly for total body 'tightness'/suffocating feeling that occurs
``` 
