PATIENT IDENTIFICATION: Ms. ***** is a 55 y.o. female who returns to our GI Oncology practice at the UCSF Comprehensive Cancer Center for follow-up of her diagnosis of metastatic <1>pancreatic adenocarcinoma</1>.     ONCOLOGIC HISTORY: Ms. ***** reports that she first notice yellowing of her urine in April 2012. She presented to the Emergency Room at ***** and was treated for a <2>urinary tract infection</2> on two separate occasions. On 07/25/2012 she presented with <3>jaundice</3>, <4>low back pain</4> and <5>pruritis</5>. A <6>CT scan</6> was performed which demonstrated a <7>pancreatic mass</7>. Ms. ***** subsequently presented to the ER at ***** with worsening <8>abdominal pain</8> and underwent a <9>procedure</9> on 08/16/2012, performed by Dr. *****. A <10>liver lesion</10> was biopsied intraoperatively and was interpreted as pathologically most consistent with <11>focal nodular hyperplasia</11>. On post-operative day 3, she developed <12>abdominal pain</12> along with profuse <13>serosanguinous drainage</13> into her <14>JP drain</14>. She became <15>hemodynamically unstable</15> (<16>hematocrit</16> dropped to <17>14.8%</17>), and was transferred to the <18>ICU</18>. On 08/19/2012, she was taken back to the OR for an <19>exploratory laparotomy</19> where <20>arterial bleeding</20> from the <21>right adrenal artery</21> and <22>dehiscence of posterior duodenojejunostomy</22> were discovered. A <23>hematoma evacuation</23>, <24>right adrenal artery cautery</24>, <25>antrectomy</25>, <26>revision gastrojejunostomy</26> were performed. She was subsequently noted to have a persistent <27>leukocytosis</27>, and a <28>urine culture</28> grew <29>E Coli</29> and <30>enterococcus species</30> for which she was treated with a course of <31>antibiotics</31>. She was extubated on 08/26/2012 and discharged on 09/15/2012. She briefly required nutritional support with <32>TPN</32> during her post-operative course which was discontinued prior to start of <33>adjuvant gemcitabine</33>.     On 10/09/2012 the patient initiated a planned 6 month course of <34>adjuvant gemcitabine chemotherapy</34> on a 3 week on, 1 week off schedule. Her Day 8 infusion was held for a
``` 
