cumulative <1>fatigue</1>, I will hold <2>treatment</2> today and ordered restaging <3>CT scans</3> to be performed. Loss of <4>appetite</4> A previous upper <5>GI series</5> demonstrated no evidence of mechanical gastric outlet obstruction, and symptoms may be in part due to <6>gastroparesis</6>, possibly due to <7>tumor infiltration</7> of the <8>celiac nerve</8> and/or loops of bowel inferior to the right hepatic lobe. She using <9>metoclopramide</9> for its pro-motility properties, and I instructed her today to increase dose to <10>10 mg</10> four times daily. She has resumed <11>megestrol acetate</11> for appetite stimulation. Patient previously did not tolerate trials of <12>Remeron</12> or <13>medicinal marijuana</13> for appetite stimulation. I provided a referral to <14>Nutrition</14> at today's visit. Pain Control Pain has remained controlled on ***** ***** dose of <15>120 mg BID</15>. She will continue ***** <16>suspension</16> as needed for breakthrough pain. We previously discussed that her pain could possibly be relieved by <17>celiac plexus block</17> if it progresses despite medical management. Insomnia She will continue to take <18>lorazepam</18> and <19>zolpidem</19> as needed for insomnia. I will plan to see Ms. ***** back following restaging <20>CT scans</20>. As always, the patient was counseled to contact the clinic or the after-hours physician on call for any new symptoms or complications in the interim between now and her follow up visit with me. Thank you for involving me in the care of this very kind patient. Please do not hesitate to contact me with any questions or concerns. I spent a total of <21>25 minutes</21> face-to-face with the patient and her family, with >50% of that time in direct counseling regarding her <22>cancer diagnosis</22>. All of the patient's questions were answered to her and her family's satisfaction.
