ner_results: ```plaintext
 review, the immunophenotype in  the current biopsy is compatible with <1>pancreatic origin</1>.The  absence of <2>TTF-1 expression</2> provides no support for a primary <3>lung adenocarcinoma</3>. Clinical and radiological correlation is  recommended.    Imaging  <4>CT CAP</4> 11/14/15  1. Postsurgical changes of distal <5>pancreatectomy</5> and <6>splenectomy</6>.   Unchanged soft tissue at the postsurgical site extending posteriorly   to surround the <7>superior mesenteric artery</7>, likely postsurgical.     2. Similar to decreased size of likely metastatic <8>mesenteric lymph nodes</8>.    3. Similar cavernous transformation of the <9>main portal vein</9> with   associated <10>varices</10>.    4. Evolving postradiation changes in the <11>left lung</11>. Nonspecific new   0.3 cm <12>pulmonary nodule</12> in the <13>lingula</13>. Attention on follow-up.     ASSESSMENT & PLAN  In summary, ***** ***** ***** ***** is a 67 y.o. male who presents to our <14>GI Oncology practice</14> at the <15>UCSF ***** ***** Family Comprehensive Cancer Center</15> for evaluation of <16>metastatic pancreatic adenocarcinoma</16>. Patient received 4 cycles of ***** in the <17>neoadjuvant setting</17> and then <18>gemcitabine</18> in the <19>adjuvant setting</19> for 6 months (completed in December 2012). He then had recurrence in the <20>lungs</20> in 2014 for which he had *****. Most recently, he has been getting therapy with <21>gemcitabine monotherapy</21> (<22>Abraxane</22> d/c'ed in July 2015 due to <23>neuropathy</23>) and has stable disease on the most recent <24>restaging scans</24> obtained on 11/14/15. His <25>CA 19-9</25> also has been declining since starting <26>gemcitabine</26> and *****-<27>paclitaxel</27> in April 2015.    At this point, he continues to be on <28>gemcitabine monotherapy</28>. I agree with omission of *****-<29>paclitaxel</29> due to the <30>grade 2 neuropathy</30>. <31>Restaging scans</31> can be obtained after 2 months of therapy (at the end of December and early January 2016) along with monthly <32>CA 19-9 levels</32> to monitor treatment response. If there is <33>disease progression</33> at that time, he can be considered for potential trials or he may be considered for <34>5FU</34>.
