 peripheral <1>groundglass</1>   ***** Posterior <2>right upper lobe consolidation</2> measuring <3>3.8 x 1.8 cm</3> (4, 120) previously <4>3.3 x 1.9 cm</4>   ***** <5>Left lower lobe nodule</5> measuring <6>1.6 x 1.5 cm</6> (4, 227) previously <7>1.6 x 1.5 cm</7>     Remaining <8>Chest</8>, <9>Abdomen</9>, <10>Pelvis</10>:   <11>Cardiovascular</11>: No large or central <12>pulmonary artery thrombus</12>. <13>Coronary artery calcifications</13>. <14>Ascending aorta</14> measures up to <15>4 cm</15> (3, 67)     <16>Lung parenchyma</16>, <17>pleura</17>, <18>airways</18>: As above. No <19>pleural effusion</19> or <20>pneumothorax</20>. Patent central airways.     <21>Chest Wall</21>: <22>Right chest wall porta catheter</22> with tip terminating in the lower <23>SVC</23>. Minimal <24>gynecomastia</24>.     <25>Liver</25> and <26>biliary system</26>: Scattered <27>hepatic low density lesions</27>, too small to characterize, likely <28>cysts</28>. <29>Hepatic vasculature</29> is patent. No <30>hydronephrosis</30>.     <31>Gallbladder</31>: Surgically absent gallbladder. Expected <32>pneumobilia</32>.     <33>Spleen</33>: The spleen is unremarkable.     <34>Pancreas</34>: Postsurgical changes of a *****. The remainder of the pancreatic body and tail are unremarkable.     <35>Adrenal glands</35>: Unremarkable.     <36>Kidneys</36>, <37>ureters</37>, <38>bladder</38>: <39>Nonobstructing renal calculi</39> bilaterally. Mild prominence of the <40>left ureter</40> with mild periureteral stranding and thickening (9, 77). The bladder is unremarkable.     <41>Gastrointestinal tract</41>: Small amount of fluid within the mid-distal <42>esophagus</42>. Within the <43>rectosigmoid colon</43> and <44>rectum</44>, there is mild mucosal thickening and multifocal narrowing (3, 235) (3, 225) (3, 226) (9, 103). There are similar findings in the distal <45>descending colon</45> (9, 87). Background of fluid-filled small bowel and colon.     No <46>bowel obstruction</46>.     <47>Peritoneal cavity</47>: Similar periaortic low density <48>1.8 cm structure</48> without <49>FDG avidity</49> (February 045). No free air or free fluid.     <50>Pelvic organs</50>: Surgically absent <51>prostate</51>. <52>Lymph nodes</52>: Multiple subcentimeter <53>mediastinal lymph nodes</53> and probable <54>pericardial recess fluid</54>. A <55>left hilar lymph node</55> measures up to <56>11 mm</56> (3, 70), difficult to compare to prior <57>PET</57>.
