ner_results: ```plaintext
 and lower lobes which has increased in size compared to 06/01/2019. For example, the <1>mass</1> in the <2>right middle lobe</2> at the level of the <3>cavoatrial junction</3> measures approximately 5.0 x 10.0 cm in maximal transverse dimensions (previously 8.1 x 4.2 cm). Similar to prior, the <4>mass</4> invades the <5>anterior chest wall</5> and <6>mediastinum</6> where it abuts the <7>right heart border</7> with loss of intervening fat plane between the <8>mass</8> and <9>right atrial blood pool</9>. The <10>mass</10> also extends to the <11>right hilum</11> where it encases but does not significantly narrow the <12>pulmonary artery</12> and <13>vein branches</13>. Increased <14>groundglass opacity</14> and <15>interlobular septal thickening</15> throughout the aerated <16>right middle</16> and <17>lower lobes</17>, compatible with worsening <18>lymphangitic spread of tumor</18>.    Increased <19>groundglass opacity</19> and <20>interlobular septal thickening</20> in the <21>left lower lobe</21> at the site of treated <22>metastasis</22> which may represent posttreatment change. Remaining <23>pulmonary nodules</23> in the <24>left lung</24> are not significantly changed.    <25>PLEURA</25>:  No <26>pleural effusion</26>. Redemonstration of diffuse <27>right pleural nodularity</27> and enhancement compatible with <28>pleural metastases</28>.    <29>MEDIASTINUM</29>:   Similar appearance of <30>right hilar lymphadenopathy</30>.    <31>HEART</31>/***** *****:  Normal <32>heart size</32>. No <33>pericardial effusion</33>. Normal caliber of the <34>aortic root</34> and <35>pulmonary artery</35>.    <36>BONES/SOFT TISSUES</36>:  Increased conspicuity of <37>sclerotic lesions</37> involving multiple <38>ribs</38>, <39>right greater than left</39>, and the <40>right inferior sternal body</40>, compatible with <41>osseous metastases</41>.    <42>IMPRESSION</42>:   1.  Worsening <43>metastatic disease</43> in the <44>right middle</44> and <45>lower lobes</45> with increased <46>tumor-related consolidation</46> and <47>lymphangitic spread of tumor</47>.    2.  Increased <48>ground glass opacity</48> in the <49>left lower lobe</49> at site of prior <50>radiation</50> which may reflect evolving posttreatment change, however progression of <51>tumor</51> is not excluded. ***** of <52>metastatic disease</52> in the <53>left lung</53> is otherwise unchanged.    3.  
``` 
