to report short period of <1>double vision</1> after waking up from nap (had taken <2>10mg compazine</2> just before). No residual <3>neurol sx</3> 09/14/20: ***** ***** ***** <4>Contrast</4>: No definite evidence of <5>intracranial metastatic disease</5>. <6>FLAIR hyperintense signal</6> along the <7>pituitary</7> ***** is of unclear etiology and may represent a <8>cystic lesion</8> as there is no definite enhancement on the postcontrast <9>T1 images</9> to suggest a <10>metastasis</10>. Recommend follow-up imaging with <11>MR sella protocol</11> in 2-4 weeks to better evaluate and assess for stability. 09/16/20: <12>Invitae germline testing</12> notable for <13>pathogenic ATM mutation</13> 09/26/20: ***** ***** 10/10/20: ***** ***** delayed due to <14>side effects</14> 10/17/20: ***** ***** (***** dose reduced by 20% to <15>120mg/m2</15>) 10/21/20: <16>MR brain</16>: normal, no <17>pituitary lesion</17> 10/31/20: <18>C4D1</18> ***** delayed per pt preference, borderline <19>plt 95</19> 11/07/20: <20>C4D1</20> ***** (***** <21>120mg/m2</21>) 11/10/20: <22>CT Chest</22>: ***** 11/11/20: <23>CT AP with Contrast</23>: Compared to 08/24/2020, decreased size of solid component and increased size of cystic component of <24>pancreatic tail mass</24>. Similar <25>vascular involvement</25> as described above. Increased <26>edema</26> and <27>stranding</27> around the <28>inferior mesenteric artery</28> and <29>inferior mesenteric veins</29>. Similar appearance of <30>small peritoneal nodules</30> and <31>small pelvic ascites</31>, again concerning for <32>peritoneal carcinomatosis</32>. Delayed <33>left nephrogram</33> with <34>urothelial enhancement</34>, similar compared to 08/24/2020. 11/21/20: ***** *****. <35>CA 19-9</35> = <36>38,423</36> 12/05/20: ***** *****
``` 
