Unremarkable Lines/drains/medical devices: None RADIATION DOSE INDICATORS: ***** *****: <1>4</1> , <2>CTDIvol Min</2>: <3>11 mGy</3>, <4>CTDIvol Max</4>: <5>21.8 mGy</5>, <6>DLP</6>: <7>1500.1 mGy.cm</7>. The following accession numbers are related to this dose report *****,***** 1. Compared to <8>08/24/2020</8>, decreased size of solid component and increased size of cystic component of <9>pancreatic tail mass</9>. Similar vascular involvement as described above. Increased <10>edema</10> and <11>stranding</11> around the <12>inferior mesenteric artery</12> and <13>inferior mesenteric veins</13>. 2. Similar appearance of small <14>peritoneal nodules</14> and small <15>pelvic ascites</15>, again concerning for <16>peritoneal carcinomatosis</16>. 3. Delayed <17>left nephrogram</17> with <18>urothelial enhancement</18>, similar compared to <19>08/24/2020</19>. Report dictated by: ***** *****, MD, signed by: ***** ***** *****, MD Department of Radiology and Biomedical Imaging <20>Ct Chest With Contrast</20> Result Date: <21>11/10/2020</21> <22>CT CHEST WITH CONTRAST</22> CLINICAL HISTORY: <23>Cancer surveillance</23> (no evidence of disease, no new symptoms) Restaging scans. <24>met pancreatic cancer</24> on ***** COMPARISON: <25>08/24/2020</25> TECHNIQUE: Serial <26>1.25 mm axial images</26> through the chest were obtained after the administration of <27>intravenous contrast</27>. RADIATION DOSE INDICATORS: ***** *****: <28>4</28> , <29>CTDIvol Min</29>: <30>11 mGy</30>, <31>CTDIvol Max</31>: <32>21.8 mGy</32>, <33>DLP</33>: <34>1500.1 mGy.cm</34> FINDINGS: <35>Right internal jugular Port-A-Cath</35> tip terminates in the upper <36>right atrium</36>. LUNGS: <37>Small nodule</37> in the <38>right middle lobe</38> appears less dense and has slightly decreased in size (series 4, image 188). Lungs otherwise clear. PLEURA: No <39>effusion</39>. MEDIASTINUM: No suspicious <40>lymph nodes</40>. HEART/***** *****: No <41>cardiomegaly</41> or <42>pericardial effusion</42>. BONES/SOFT TISSUES: <43>Suspicious lesions</43>. VISIBLE ABDOMEN: Please see separate abdomen/pelvis CT report of the same date.<44>3 mm nodule</44> in the <45>right middle lobe</45> has decreased in attenuation since the previous exam. No new or increasing <46>metastatic disease</46> in the chest. Report dictated
