ner_results: ```plaintext
 is a new component extending into the right <1>psoas musculature</1> (*****/*****). Additionally, the <2>collection</2> abuts and exerts mass effect on the <3>ascending colon</3> (*****/*****) and makes broad contact with the second through fourth portions of the <4>duodenum</4>. <5>Air</5> noted within the <6>collection</6>. Mild-moderate right <7>hydronephrosis</7> with differential enhancement of the right <8>kidney</8> compared, new compared to 02/12/2021 and increasing compared to 02/15/2021, probably related to surrounding <9>inflammation</9>. <10>Adrenal Glands</10>:  Unremarkable <11>Kidneys</11>:  Mild-moderate right <12>hydronephrosis</12>, new compared to 02/12/2021 and increasing compared to 08/06/2020, likely related to inflammatory change from adjacent <13>peripancreatic fluid collection</13>. <14>GI Tract</14>:  <15>Peripancreatic fluid collection</15> contacting the <16>ascending colon</16> and <17>duodenum</17> described above. <18>Vasculature</18>:  Unremarkable <19>Lymphadenopathy</19>: Described above. <20>Peritoneum</20>: Trace free fluid.     1.  <21>Hypermetabolic pancreatic head mass</21> status post <22>metal biliary drain placement</22>. Evaluation of locoregional extent of <23>disease</23> is limited by surrounding <24>peripancreatic fluid collection</24>. 2.  Within this limitation, no clear nodal or distant <25>metastatic disease</25>. Unchanged ***** small <26>periportal lymph node</26>. Scattered small <27>pulmonary nodules</27> are unchanged. Unchanged ***** <28>T5 vertebral body lucent lesion</28>. 3.  Decreased size of <29>peripancreatic fluid collection</29> status post <30>percutaneous drainage placement</30>. However, there is a new component of the <31>collection</31> involving the right <32>psoas muscle</32>, new <33>air</33> within the <34>collection</34>, and increasing right <35>hydronephrosis</35> likely related to adjacent <36>inflammation</36>. The <37>collection</37> makes broad contact with the <38>duodenum</38> and, to a lesser extent, the <39>ascending colon</39>. While <40>air</40> within the <41>collection</41> is likely related to instrumentation, <42>fluoroscopic tube check</42> or repeat <43>CT abdomen pelvis with oral contrast</43> could be obtained to evaluate for <44>fistula</44>. 4.  For further detail on simultaneously acquired <45>PET/CT</45>, see separately dictated report.    <46>CT Abdomen /Pelvis with Contrast</46>
