<1>pancreatic mass</1>, along with <2>pulmonary findings</2> c/w <3>mild heart failure</3>, while her <4>tumor markers</4>-9 levels declined to normal range. ***** went on to complete a course ***** ***** (<5>Cyberknife</5>) through early <6>March 2019</6>, with the decision not to pursue <7>surgery</7> thereafter due ***** <8>co-morbidities</8> (particularly her underlying <9>cardiac issues</9>) *****. By *****, f/u <10>surveillance imaging</10> ***** evidence of <11>locoregional disease progression</11> as well ***** <12>metastases</12>, for which ***** restarted *****, ***** *****/<13>paclitaxel</13> at a ***** dosing schedule and at reduced doses of both agents (plus ***** <14>prophylaxis</14>). ***** a/***** on, due to recurrent <15>cardiac issues</15> (not clearly attribute to her <16>chemotherapy</16>) ***** <17>toxicity</17>. After <18>5.5 cycles</18>, interval <19>re-imaging</19> ***** good <20>disease control</20>, while <21>tumor markers</21>-9 remained within normal range. *****, her regimen was ***** <22>gemcitabine</22> alone as a form of '<23>maintenance treatment</23>' (continuing with the ***** dosing schedule, i.e. <24>days 1 and 15 of a 28-day cycle</24>) for several additional cycles, before taking a <25>chemotherapy holiday</25> starting in late <26>August 2020</26>. During her treatment-free interval over the next several months, she developed both <27>locoregional</27> and (modest) <28>hepatic disease progression</28>, resulting in <29>biliary obstruction</29> that has necessitated ***** <30>stenting</30> of both the <31>L and R intrahepatic biliary systems</31>, with multiple exchanges since then in the context of recurrent <32>cholangitis</32>. Repeat <33>ERCPs</33> will be scheduled at ***** in an additional <34>4-6 weeks' time</34>; she was counselled to watch for signs/sxs of recurrent <35>biliary infectious</35> in the meantime. She is now back on <36>chemotherapy</36> consisting of ***** reduced-dose <37>gemcitabine</37>/*****-<38>paclitaxel</38>. Treatment has been interrupted on a couple of occasions due to <39>hospital</39>
