ner_results: ```plaintext
 the first-line treatment of <1>metastatic pancreatic cancer</1>, and he was sent consent forms for both of these ahead of time to review:  (1) the ***** trial, a randomized phase II trial evaluating the combination of <2>gemcitabine</2> plus <3>*****-paclitaxel</3> with or without *****-*****, a bispecific monoclonal antibody directed against <4>IGF-1R</4> and *****. For this study, patients are initially screened by measurement of <5>serum free IGF-1 levels</5>, as only those with high <6>IGF-1 levels</6> are randomized. The study also requires <7>tumor tissue</7> for assessment of intratumoral <8>Heregulin (HRG) expression</8>, although there is no cutoff for study eligibility. ***** the nature of <9>clinical trial</9> and specifically the study rationale, treatment regimen, screening tests and logistics of the above <10>clinical trial</10>.   (2) a phase II trial consisting of the combination of <11>gemcitabine</11>/<12>*****-paclitaxel</12> plus <13>ibrutinib</13>.    After much discussion and consideration, the patient is inclined to move ahead with <14>SOC chemotherapy</14> with *****. He is in fact already scheduled to have a <15>Mediport</15> placed through his local oncologist tomorrow, and will let us know w/i the next day or so whether he wishes to receive his treatment locally vs here at *****.    The other issues we covered included:  - <16>Pain management</16>: A new script for ***** ***** was provided for <17>long-acting RTC pain control</17>. Future consideration could be made for <18>EUS-guided celiac plexus nerve block</18> as well if he does not respond adequate to <19>opioid analgesics</19>.  - Given his young age at presentation, I will make a referral for him to be seen at our <20>Cancer Risk program</20> for <21>genetic counseling</21>, despite the absence of a family history of cancer.  - The patient does have some pain referrable to the <22>sacrum</22>, with <23>PET</23> and <24>MRI</24> suggesting some <25>osseous metastases</25> in that area. For now, I will see how this responds to <26>systemic therapy</26>, but we could consider <27>spot RT</27> to that area in the future.    All of the patient's questions 
 were answered to his and his partner's satisfaction. If he chooses to receive his care at ***** we will get him set up to start within the next week or so.  
``` 
