ner_results: ```plaintext
For example, previously identified <1>hepatic segment 2 lesion</1> now measures 1.2 x 1.7 cm (series 7, image 27), previously 1.4 x 1.6 cm. <2>Hepatic segment 5 lesion</2> measures 1.5 x 1.2 cm (series 7, image 70), previously 1.6 x 1.3 cm. <3>Gallbladder</3>: Air-fluid level is noted within nondistended gallbladder. The common wall abuts the hepatic segment 5 lesion as described but no evidence of gallbladder wall involvement. Unchanged <4>CBD stent placement</4> with similar <5>pneumobilia</5> and mild <6>intrahepatic biliary dilatation</6>. <7>Spleen</7>: Unremarkable <8>Pancreas</8>: The <9>infiltrate necrotic primary pancreatic head mass</9> is difficult to assess for exact measurement but qualitatively has increased in size (series 7, image 41) from prior exam 08/01/2019 especially the anterior centrally necrotic component. Similar involvement of the adjacent <10>transverse duodenum</10>, with similar degree of <11>pancreatic ductal dilatation</11> and <12>pancreatic tail atrophy</12>. The degree of <13>SMV narrowing</13> is similar with resulting moderate or severe <14>stenosis</14> (series 604, image 58). Similar <15>SMA</15> and main <16>portal vein encasement</16>. <17>Adrenal Glands</17>: Unremarkable <18>Kidneys</18>: Unremarkable <19>GI Tract</19>: Unremarkable <20>Vasculature</20>: Unremarkable <21>Lymphadenopathy</21>: Unchanged mildly prominent subcentimeter <22>peripancreatic lymph nodes</22>. <23>Peritoneum</23>: No <24>ascites</24> <25>Bladder</25>: Unremarkable <26>Reproductive organs</26>: Unremarkable <27>Bones</27>: No suspicious lesions <28>Extraperitoneal soft tissues</28>: Unremarkable <29>Lines/drains/medical devices</29>: None <30>RADIATION DOSE INDICATORS</30>: ***** *****: 4 , <31>CTDIvol Min</31>: 9.1 mGy, <32>CTDIvol Max</32>: 19.8 mGy, <33>DLP</33>: 1298.7 mGy.cm. The following accession numbers are related to this dose report *****,***** 1. Interval increase in size of primary infiltrative necrotic pancreatic head mass. 2. Similar in size and appearance of multiple <34>hepatic metastases</34>. Report dictated by: ***** ***** *****, DO, signed by: ***** ***** *****, MD Department of Radiology and Biomedical Imaging <35>Ct Chest With</35>
``` 
