ner_results: ```plaintext
female who presents to our GI Oncology practice at the UCSF ***** ***** Family Comprehensive Cancer Center for a follow-up visit of <1>metastatic pancreatic adenocarcinoma</1> with <2>biopsy proven liver metastasis</2>. Patient was started on ***** <3>06/07/19</3> and has been tolerating it well with dose reduction of <4>irinotecan</4> by 20% starting with <5>cycle 2</5>. Her <6>restaging scans</6> from <7>08/01/2019</7> showed increase in the size of the <8>hepatic lesions</8>. However, the scans were compared to <9>05/17/19</9> which was prior to the start of <10>chemotherapy</10> on <11>06/07/19</11>. For this reason, we recommended to continue on ***** as we were not certain if this is true progression due to the lag time between the comparator scan and the current scan. She continued to have clinical decline with worsening <12>fatigue</12> and also <13>weight loss</13>. She requested a week delay in <14>chemotherapy</14> which has helped with her symptoms. She has now completed <15>7 cycles of chemotherapy</15>. Her most recent <16>restaging scans</16> from <17>09/18/19</17> showed overall <18>stable disease</18> in the liver but increase in the size of the <19>pancreatic primary</19>. I called and spoke with the radiologist to get a better understanding of the <20>primary pancreatic tumor characterization</20>. He noted that there is increased enhancement around the tumor so concerning for <21>progressive disease</21>. As her ***** has not decreased either and she has had a difficult time tolerating this regimen, my recommendation is to switch her therapy to <22>gemcitabine</22> combined with *****-<23>paclitaxel</23>. I reviewed the potential side effects of this regimen including but not limited to: <24>neuropathy</24>, <25>cytopenias</25> increasing the risk of <26>infections</26> and <27>bleeding</27>, requirements for <28>blood transfusions</28>, <29>alopecia</29>, <30>rash</30>, <31>edema</31>, <32>fatigue</32>, <33>infusion reaction</33>, <34>nausea/vomiting</34>, <35>myalgias</35>. She will also undergo formal <36>chemo teach</36> prior to starting. -plan for <37>gemcitabine 1000 mg/m2</37> + *****-<38>paclitaxel 125 mg/m2</38> on days 1, 8, 15 out of <39>28-day cycle</39>. -We will plan for a <40>CT chest</40>,
``` 
