 abdomen and pelvis to be obtained after <1>2 months</1> of <2>therapy</2> and will monitor ***** <3>levels</3> monthly.     I reviewed the <4>scan results</4> and these recommendations with the patient and her family during today's visit. I provided them with an opportunity to ask questions and I believe that all of their questions have been answered to their satisfaction.     <5>#R shoulder and arm limited ROM</5> and <6>decreased strength</6>: Continues   - <7>MRI</7> from <8>July 23</8> showed: <9>Moderate grade articular sided tear of the subscapularis</9>, <10>articular sided tear of the supraspinatus</10>, <11>subacromial subdeltoid bursitis</11>, and <12>degenerative tearing of the superior ***** extending into the biceps *****</12>.  - An external referral to <13>ortho</13> was placed during prior visit.    <14># Supportive care</14>:   - Continue <15>ondansetron</15> and <16>Compazine</16> alternatively to better manage her <17>nausea</17>.     <18>#Follow-up</18>: <19>2 weeks</19> when she is due for *****  As always, we reminded the patient to call us with any questions or concerns in the meantime.      I performed this <20>consultation</20> using real-time <21>Telehealth tools</21>, including a live video connection between my location and the patient's location. Prior to initiating the consultation, I obtained informed verbal consent to perform this consultation using Telehealth tools and answered all the questions about the Telehealth interaction.    ***** *****, MD, MS  Clinical Assistant Professor in ***** *****   UCSF ***** ***** Family Comprehensive Cancer Center      
