<1>diff</1>, <2>LFTs</2>, <3>chemistry panel</3> and <4>CA 19-9</4> prior to his first cycle of <5>chemotherapy</5>. As the patient has a strong family history of <6>cancer</6> and due to his young age at diagnosis, we will request assistance from our <7>genetic counselors</7> for evaluation of a possible hereditary <8>pancreatic cancer syndromes</8>. We have placed a referral to our <9>Cancer Center dietician</9> for weight maintenance. We will provide a prescription of <10>antiemetics</10> and <11>anti-diarrheal medications</11> prior to the initiation of the <12>chemotherapy</12>. I provided handouts on <13>chemotherapy regimen</13> details and provided him with an opportunity to ask questions. I believe that I was able to answer all of his questions to his satisfaction. He will return to ***** ***** in clinic after the <14>pathology</14> from the <15>biopsy</15> is available. #<16>Hyperbilirubinemia</16>: <17>T. Bili 1.9</17> on prior <18>labs</18>; we will get <19>labs</19> prior to next visit to make sure that there is not further increase in <20>bilirubin</20>. If there is worsening <21>hyperbilirubinemia</21>, we will have to obtain <22>imaging</22> to evaluate for biliary ***** and potential <23>ERCP</23> for consideration of <24>stent placement</24>. #<25>HTN</25>: Not well-controlled today. He didn't take <26>lisinopril</26> this morning. -I recommended that the patient take the <27>lisinopril</27> today and daily as prescribed by his <28>PCP</28>. We provided the patient with information regarding our clinic hours, phone number, important details of precautions during <29>therapy</29>. I provided them with an opportunity to ask questions and I believe that all of their questions have been answered to their satisfaction. We encouraged him to contact us with any questions or concerns. I would be happy to see the patient back in my clinic at any point in the future. Thank you for the opportunity to participate in the care of this kind patient. Please feel free to call me at any time at *****-*****-***** if you have any questions about the <30>treatment</30>, my recommendations, or if I can be of any assistance in the future. *****, ***** *****, MD, MS Clinical Assistant Professor of Medicine Department of Medicine, Division of Oncology UCSF ***** ***** Family Comprehensive Cancer Center 12/25/2015
