ner_results: ```plaintext
 quadrant. Pancreas: <1>Resection of the pancreatic body and tail</1>. Adrenal Glands: <2>1.3 cm hypodense nodule</2> within the right adrenal gland is unchanged compared to 01/10/2012 Kidneys: <3>Subcentimeter hypoattenuating lesions</3> left kidney, too small to characterize, stable. Vasculature: <4>IVC filter</4> in place. GI Tract: Unremarkable Pelvis: <5>Prominent pelvic veins</5> compatible with <6>pelvic congestion syndrome</6>. Lymphadenopathy: Absent Ascites: Absent Bones: No suspicious lesions     IMPRESSION: There are <7>7 hypervascular lesions</7> with the liver. Some of the lesions demonstrate interval increase in size while others are decreased in size compared to most recent prior. This could reflect a mixed response to treatment versus differences in technique between studies. No new lesions are seen.       Impression and Recommendations:  In summary, Ms. ***** is a 56 y.o. female with <8>oligometastatic liver disease</8> from a <9>non-functioning PNET</9>, with evidence of good durable disease control and reasonably good (in fact, improved) tolerance on current <10>everolimus</10> at reduced doses of <11>7.5 mg daily</11>. We discussed the following issues and plan:    - Watch for signs/sxs of <12>recurrent bowel obstruction</12>.  - My review of her most recent <13>CT scans</13> show essentially stable disease, with minimal growth in some measurable lesions ***** by similar degree of reduction in others. We will continue to image at approx <14>6 month intervals</14>.  - She should continue with q3-4 month labs including <15>CBC</15>, <16>LFTs</16>, <17>creatinine</17>, <18>glucose</18>, <19>PO4</19>, and <20>cholesterol panel</20>.  - Recent <21>Endocrinology evaluation</21> for <22>diabetic management</22>, presumably prompted by <23>everolimus</23>; discussed potential plan to start <24>non-insulin pharmacologic rx</24> in the future. Patient is following <25>blood sugars</25> at home.  - No plans for repeat <26>locoregional ablative/embolization therapy</26> in immediate future.
``` 
