History of Present Illness  09/12/19: Local ED with 1mo <1>abdominal bloating</1>, <2>weight loss</2> *****, <3>dark urine</3> and <4>light stools</4>  US: <5>Fatty liver</5>, no malignancy in liver.  Interval <6>bilary ductal distension</6>  CT A/P: <7>Distended gallbladder</7> as well <8>dilated intra and extrahepatic bile ducts</8> with abrupt transition point at the ampulla raising the concern for <9>choledocholithiasis</9> versus <10>malignancy</10>  09/13/19: <11>EGD/EUS</11>: An irregular oval <12>mass</12> was identified in the <13>pancreatic head</13> at the head/neck junction. The mass was <14>hypoechoic</14>. The mass measured <15>25 mm by 18 mm</15> in maximal cross-sectional diameter. The endosonographic borders were *****.  There was sonographic evidence suggesting <16><180 degree involvement of the portal vein, splenoportal confluence and SMV</16>, over a length of <17>-15 mm</17>.   <18>FNA path</18>: <19>Adenocarcinoma</19>  09/13/19: <20>ERCP</20>: Two <21>10 mm by 4 cm uncovered metal stents</21> were placed into the <22>common bile duct</22> across the stricture (the first stent did not fully traverse the stricture, so a 2nd overlapping stent was placed)  Discharged 09/13/19  09/21/19: <23>CA 19-9</23>: <24>49</24>, <25>AST</25> <26>29</26>, <27>ALT</27> <28>111</28>, <29>Tbili</29> <30>0.6</30>  09/28/19: <31>CA 19-9</31>: <32>84</32>  09/28/19: <33>CT Chest</33> (UCSF): *****   09/28/19: <34>CT AP Pancreatic Protocol</34> (UCSF): <35>Ill defined hypodense mass</35> in the <36>pancreatic uncinate process</36> measures up to <37>2.5 cm</37>, consistent with known <38>pancreatic adenocarcinoma</38>. The mass abuts the <39>main portal vein</39> and <40>superior mesenteric vein</40> at the <41>portal-SMV confluence</41>. Several small <42>subcentimeter hypodense lesions</42> in the <43>pancreatic parenchyma</43>. The several of these lesions are favored to reflect <44>small cysts</44>. However there is an <45>Indeterminate lesion</45> in <46>hepatic segment June 24</46> measures <47>18 mm</47>. Recommend further evaluation with <48>MR liver examination</48>
``` 
