03/05/20: Restarted treatment ***** *****  03/19/20: ***** *****  *****/*****/*****-*****/*****/*****: Hospitalized with <1>abdominal pain</1> and found to have <2>gallbladder fossa abscess</2> and <3>Klebsiella bacteremia</3> s/p <4>percutaneous drain placement</4> 03/28/20.  Also received <5>Zosyn</5>, transitioned to <6>Augmentin</6> to complete total <7>14d course</7> on 04/10/20.  04/25/20: <8>Percutaneous drain</8> was removed by *****  05/02/20: C4D1 *****  05/19/20: ***** *****  06/04/20: <9>CT CAP</9>: <10>stable disease</10>, resolved <11>abdominal fluid collection</11>  06/06/20: ***** *****  06/20/20: ***** *****. Patient experienced <12>grade 2 reaction</12> during <13>oxaliplatin infusion</13>. <14>Benadryl 25mg IV</14> was administered, and the patient reported near immediate relief. Patient tolerated the <15>infusion re-challenge</15> up to ***** rate. He completed the <16>oxaliplatin</16> without further incident. <17>CA 19-9</17> = <18>136</18>  07/04/20: ***** ***** ***** <19>19-9=93</19>  07/16/20: <20>CT CAP pancreatic protocol</20>: <21>Stable disease</21>.   08/12/20: ***** with <22>PV resection</22>. Post op course c/b prolonged hospital stay due to <23>ileus</23> and <24>delayed gastric emptying</24>, <25>aspiration pneumonia</25>, and <26>pancreatic leak</26>. Post op <27>ileus</27> and ***** required prolonged <28>bowel rest</28>, <29>parenteral nutrition</29>, and <30>NG placement</30> multiple times. <31>Reglan</31> was added to his medications and his diet was slowly advanced to a <32>minced diet</32> with <33>nectar thick</33> ***** September 01. He also developed <34>aspiration PNA</34> and was found to have <35>right vocal cord paralysis</35> during evaluation by <36>OHNS</36>.  Also c/b infected <37>pancreatic leak</37> s/p <38>IR drain</38> and required <39>IV antibiotics</39>.  Discharged 09/08/20 to ***** <40>SNF</40> with <41>drain</41>, <42>TPN</42> and <43>IV abx</43>   10/20/20: <44>Drain removal</44>
``` 
