<1>hepaticojejunostomy</1>, with the hepatic limb of the *****-en-Y appearing dilated and fluid-filled measuring up to 3.5 cm, new compared to 01/05/2021. There is narrowing of the hepatic limb at the presumed <2>anastomotic site</2> (series 3, image 84). <3>Dilatation of the proximal jejunum</3> up to 4.2 cm, and another site of narrowing within the <4>efferent loop</4> (series 3, image 80), distal to which the <5>jejunum</5> is decompressed. No evidence of <6>bowel ischemia</6>. <7>Metallic stent</7> is now seen in the <8>jejunum</8> distal to the area of narrowing. Vasculature: Ill-defined soft tissue between the <9>IVC</9> and <10>celiac</10>. Unchanged occlusion at the ***** confluence with extensive collaterals. The native left and right <11>portal veins</11> remain patent but similar to size with the collaterals. Moderate <12>atherosclerotic disease</12> of the <13>abdominal aorta</13> and its branches. Lymphadenopathy: Absent Peritoneum: Increased <14>ascites</14>, but small in volume. Bladder: ***** Reproductive organs: <15>Prostatomegaly</15> Bones: No suspicious lesions. Multilevel <16>degenerative disease</16> of the <17>thoracolumbar spine</17>. Extraperitoneal soft tissues: Unremarkable Lines/drains/medical devices: As above RADIATION DOSE INDICATORS: ***** *****: 3 , <18>CTDIvol Min</18>: 6 mGy, <19>CTDIvol Max</19>: 6 mGy, <20>DLP</20>: 310.5 mGy.cm 1. <21>Dilation of the proximal jejunum</21> measuring up to 4.2 cm, with 2 foci of narrowing as detailed above, distal to which the <22>jejunum</22> with decompressed. Findings are concerning for <23>small bowel obstruction</23>. There is no evidence of <24>bowel ischemia</24>. 2. Free-floating <25>metallic stent</25> in the stomach and a second <26>metallic stent</26> within the segment of mid <27>jejunum</27> distal to the point of <28>bowel obstruction</28>. 3. Small <29>subsegmental pulmonary embolism</29> in the <30>right lower lobe</30>. 4. Similar appearance of ill-defined soft tissue surrounding the <31>IVC</31> and the <32>celiac axis</32>, which could represent postsurgical scarring versus local <33>tumor recurrence</33>. 5. Increased <34>ascites</34>, but small in volume. //Impression January 19
``` 
