 this time, it was recommended that he proceed with <1>gemcitabine</1> plus *****-<2>paclitaxel</2> for up to 4-6 months.  <3>C1D1</3> *****/<4>abraxane</4>=10/19/19.   Given older age, I empirically modified regimen to be given D1,15 ***** with ***** 20% dose reduced to <5>800mg/m2</5>.    12/07/19 <6>CT AP</6> demonstrated growth of a segment June 24 lesion <7>3cm</7> from <8>0.8cm</8> on 09/28/19, however stable pancreatic primary.  Notably <9>CA 19-9</9> had also ***** from <10>88</10> to <11>130</11> (nadir <12>63</12> on October 19 and baseline <13>84</13> on September 28).  Pt also poorly tolerated ***** with drug related <14>fevers</14> for most of the cycle. He was recommended to switch to *****. <15>C1D1</15> 12/29/19, c/b <16>gangrenous cholecystitis</16> s/p <17>cholecystectomy</17> 01/04/20. 02/13/19 post operative scans demonstrated ***** in chest, stable pancreatic lesion, and hepatic ***** lesion that was previously describe as a <18>metastasis</18>, on look back by radiology, is felt to represent sequela (scar) from resolved <19>abscess</19> and NOT metastasis. Discussed with IR and Dr. *****: no biopsy, and can still plan for surgery after <20>neoadjuvant chemotherapy</20>.     Hospitalized again *****/*****-*****/*****/***** with <21>gallbladder fossa abscess</21>, s/p <22>IR drain placement</22> (now also s/p drain removal 04/25/20) and <23>14d antibiotics</23> until 04/10/20 (now complete). <24>C4</24> ***** was delayed as a result. Completed <25>8 cycles</25> of ***** (*****=07/06/20) with stable disease on scans.    Now s.p ***** with <26>PV reconstruction</26> 08/12/20 with complicated post op course and prolonged hospitalization as detailed in ***** (<27>anastomotic leak</27> s/p <28>IR drain</28>, <29>infected fluid</29> ***** s/p <30>IV abx</30>, <31>aspiration pna</31>, <32>vocal cord paralysis</32> requiring <33>TPN</33>). He is clinically improving.  Scans 12/03/20 demonstrated no clear evidence of recurrence though he had increased soft tissue in surgical bed that could be post op but warrants close follow up. <34>PE</34> found on 12/03/20 scans and started on <35>Xarelto</35>. Since then he has been hospitalized 4 times, as detailed above in *****, with ***** x2 ***** switched to <36>Lovenox</36>, then stopped <37>anticoagulation</37>.
