Imaging  <1>PET/CT</1> 09/16/2012  <2>Dilatation of the pancreatic duct body and tail</2>.  There is a <3>cystic area</3> proximal to this area.  No <4>FDG PET activity</4> but present <5>CT scan findings</5> are suggestive of <6>recurrent neoplasm</6>.  Increased <7>FDG uptake</7> within the <8>L2 vertebral body</8> <9>SUV 4.9</9>.  This corresponds to a <10>sclerotic lesion</10> in the right portion of the posterior vertebral body measuring <11>1.3 x 1.5 x 1.7 cm</11>.  This is consistent with a <12>sclerotic metastasis</12>.  There is <13>focal increased FDG uptake</13> <14>SUV 3.3</14> in the <15>left periaortic region</15> corresponding to a <16>soft tissue nodular lesion</16> measuring <17>1.5 x 1.4 cm</17>.  The findings are suspicious for <18>metastatic lymphadenopathy</18>.  The <19>nodes</19> are inferior to the <20>pancreas</20> and at the level of the lower panel of the <21>left kidney</21>.  There is <22>mild FDG uptake</22> within the <23>right hilar lymph node</23> next <24>SUV 3.1</24> as well as within the <25>left peritracheal lymph nodes</25> <26>SUV 2.9</26>.  The area of uptake in the <27>PET scan</27> in the <28>right hilum</28> measures <29>1.6 x 1.2 cm</29>.  The area of uptake in the <30>left periaortic region</30> measures roughly <31>0.6 x 2.2 cm</31>.  There was a <32>0.3 x 0.4 cm soft tissue attenuation nodule</32> in the <33>right lower lobe</33> immediately posterior to the <34>minor fissure</34> in the <35>anterior segment</35>.    <36>CT abdomen and pelvis</36> 08/31/2012  <37>1.7 cm cystic structures</37> seen in the region of the <38>pancreatic body</38>.
``` 
