ner_results: ```plaintext
 of intravascular <1>tumor growth</1>.   However, areas of the main <2>tumor mass</2> such as A11 show similar  architectural properties, with <3>malignant cells</3> arranged in dilated  channels and surrounding by fibrous stroma. A6 shows mucin within a  <4>lymph node</4>, raising the possibility of <5>lymph node spread</5>.   <6>Immunohistochemical</6>, <7>in situ hybridization</7>, or <8>histochemical stains</8> were  necessary to evaluate this case and establish the correct <9>diagnosis</9>.   The following <10>stains</10> were performed and evaluated at ***** on block A6:    - <11>CD31</11>: Highlights <12>vascular endothelium</12>, does not show intravascular  <13>tumor</13>. This focus is interpreted as <14>invasive tumor</14> in <15>peripancreatic  soft tissue</15>.   - <16>Keratin</16>: ***** single <17>tumor cells</17> and small clusters of <18>cells</18> less  than 0.2 mm in greatest diameter in association with <19>mucin</19> in a <20>lymph  node</20>. An additional <21>H&E recut</21> shows similar features. May represent  in-transit <22>isolated tumor cells</22>. This is an evolving area as far as  clinical significance.    <23>MMR proteins</23> all intact by <24>IHC</24>.  ---------------------------------------------  His <25>postoperative course</25> was notable for <26>fevers</26> of unclear etiology, <27>rx'ed empirically with IV antibiotics/anti-fungal rx</27>; a <28>Hgb</28> that ***** at 6.2 for which he received <29>2u PRBCs</29>; and <30>insulin ggt</30> transitioned to a <31>subcutaneous regimen</31> prior to discharge.     He did require <32>hospital re-admission</32> from January 16 - 01/19/2019 due to <33>abdominal pain</33>.***** during this ***** a widely patent <34>anastomosis</34>, some mild <35>inflammation</35> around the <36>anastamosis</36> with no <37>ulceration</37>, ***** <38>gastropathy</38>. <39>Biopsies</39> were ***** no <40>malignancy</40> identified. He ***** on *****, a <41>PPI</41>, and <42>triple therapy</42> for <43>H.pylori</43> (although <44>bx results</44> showed no organisms).     <45>CT scans</45> performed during <46>admission</46> showed ***** ***** new <47>2.3 cm hepatic metastasis</47> in segment 8, along with extensive <48>peritoneal stranding</48> and <49>nodularity</49> of indeterminate significance.
