separately dictated report from the CT of the chest of the same date. Liver: Similar severe diffuse <1>hepatic steatosis</1>, which decreases sensitivity for detection of <2>hepatic metastases</2>. Gallbladder: Unremarkable Spleen: Unremarkable Pancreas: Similar appearance of locally advanced <3>pancreatic cancer</3> which encases the <4>celiac axis</4> and branches as well as the <5>superior mesenteric artery</5>, as described vascular section. Exact dimensions of the masses difficult given its infiltrative nature, however it measures approximately 3.5 x 4.7 cm in the AP and transverse dimensions. Adrenal Glands: Similar left <6>adrenal gland thickening</6>. Kidneys: Unremarkable GI Tract: Diffuse thickening of the <7>ascending colon</7>, similar to multiple prior examinations. This may relate to edema/venous congestion from <8>portal occlusion</8>. Vasculature: Similar appearance of occluded main <9>portal vein</9> with <10>cavernous transformation</10>. Again seen is attenuated appearance of the encased portion of the <11>splenic artery</11>. Additional celiac axis branches are not seen and may be occluded as a result of surrounding tumor invasion. Lymphadenopathy: Absent Peritoneum: No ascites Bladder: Unremarkable Reproductive organs: Unremarkable Bones: Similar multilevel <12>degenerative changes</12> within the visualized spine. Extraperitoneal soft tissues: Unremarkable Lines/drains/medical devices: None RADIATION DOSE INDICATORS: ***** *****: 4 , <13>CTDIvol Max</13>: 14.6 mGy, <14>DLP</14>: 1001.5 mGy.cm. The following accession numbers are related to this dose report *****,***** 1. Similar appearance of locally advanced pancreatic cancer with encasement of adjacent vasculature, as detailed in body of report. 2. Diffuse thickening of the ascending colon with improved thickening of the proximal transverse colon. Findings are favored to represent <15>portal colopathy</15> rather than <16>colitis</16> given chronicity and portal vein occlusion. 3. Severe hepatic steatosis, as before, which decreases
``` 
