- Some cumulative <1>fatigue</1> a/w <2>treatment</2>; still independent with <3>ADLs</3> 
- No <4>nausea</4>, but some <5>dysgeusia</5> causing diminished <6>appetite</6> 
- ~5 kg down from baseline, but now stable 
- <7>Constipation</7> following each <8>chemotherapy infusion</8>; uses <9>laxatives</9> regularly 
- <10>Blood sugars</10> reasonably well controlled on current <11>insulin regimen</11>, although does get in the <12>200s range</12> in the AM 
- No <13>urinary difficulties</13> 
- No <14>angina</14>/<15>cardiac symptoms</15> 
- No <16>abdominal pain</16> 
- No <17>febrile complications</17> during <18>chemotherapy</18> 
- Mild chronic <19>dry cough</19> 
- Chronic <20>loss of hearing</20> in <21>R ear</21> (following <22>ear infection</22> in 2016) 
- Some <23>L UE neuropathy</23> since <24>surgery</24> 
- Moderate <25>hair loss</25> 
- No evidence of <26>depression</26> or <27>psychosis</27> 

The remainder of a full review of systems was negative. 

PAST MEDICAL AND SURGICAL HISTORY 

