ner_results: ```plaintext
bloody stools x 1. <1>Hgb</1> ***** at <2>6.6</2>, for which she was tx'ed with <3>2u PRBCs</3>. <4>EGD</4> notable for the following: 1. The <5>duodenum</5> was mildly edematous with some distortion of the lumen. <6>Biliary stent</6> appeared to be pressing against the ***** wall of the duodenum with an area of <7>ulceration</7> but no visible bleeding or blood vessel. There were a few tiny ***** in the duodenum likely from prior radiation. <8>APC</8> was performed at <9>15 Watts</9> of two small spots in the duodenum. 2. The previously visualized <10>pyloric channel ulcer</10> was still present, clean based with no visible vessel or bleeding. In the <11>antrum</11> there was a small amount of ***** likely from prior radiation, treated with <12>APC</12> at <13>15 watts</13> with good effect. 3. The previously placed <14>gastrojejunostomy stent</14> was in place and patent. 4. The mucosa of the <15>esophagus</15> appeared normal. The patient was otherwise managed symptomatically, with her anticoagulation changed from ***** to <16>Apixaban</16>. D/c'ed to home on <17>11/21/2021</17>. Did require additional <18>1u PRBC</18> on <19>11/27/2021</19> for <20>Hgb</20> of <21>8.2</21> and another episode of bloody stools. She was then readmitted to ***** on <22>12/04/2021</22> for <23>hypotension</23>, <24>hematemesis</24>; rx'ed with <25>FFP</25>, <26>2u PRBCs</26>, <27>octreotide</27>, <28>IV protonix</28>. Also underwent <29>CT angiogram</29> of the <30>brain/neck</30> due to <31>slurred speech</31>/<32>R UE motor weakness</32>, found to have <33>L precentral gyrus CVA</33>. D/c'ed to home on <34>12/07/2021</34>. - <35>12/24/2021</35>: Discussed at ***** ***** clinic visit her <36>GoC</36> given her marginal functional status to consider further cancer treatment. Ultimately enrolled on <37>home hospice</37>, but this was revoked so she could undergo repeat <38>CT scans</38> and receive additional supportive care at our <39>infusion center</39> - Repeat imaging (<40>CT scans</40> <41>01/16/2022</41>) with stable <42>1o pancreatic mass</42>, no evidence of progression. - Due to gradually worsening <43>abdominal pain</43>, repeat <44>CT scans</44> (non-contrast) were performed on <45>04/13/2022</45>, with stable to minimal progression in her <46>pancreatic head</46>
``` 
