February 2014: in *****, <1>epigastric</1> and <2>RUQ pain</2>, and a <3>CT</3> (+) <4>mass</4> in the <5>head of the pancreas</5> (2 cm). <6>EUS</6> with <7>FNA</7>(+) <8>neuroendocrine tumor</8>. She was told at that time it was inoperable. <9>EUS</9> 02/18/2014 (***** *****): (Report only) <10>multiple acute duodenal ulcers</10>, <11>3.5 cm hypoechoic infiltrative lesion</11> at <12>pancreatic head</12> encasing the <13>CBD</13>, <14>SMV</14>/<15>portal vein</15> and *****. <16>Dilated proximal biliary tree</16> and <17>distended GB</17>. <18>LDA</18> around ***** and <19>SMA</19>. <20>FNA</20> 02/18/2014 (***** *****): <21>Bx</21> shows "some lesional cells positive for <22>insulin</22>. <23>PET CT</23> body 03/21/2014 (***** *****): (report only) increased <24>FDG uptake</24> in <25>pancreatic head</25> and <26>body</26> near the resection; suspicious for <27>recurrent tumor</27>. <28>Markedly dilated CBD</28>, possibly due to <29>distal obstruction</29>. <30>Small non-FDG avid groundglass opacity</30> in <31>L upper lung lobe</31>, indeterminate but <32>inflammatory</32> > <33>neoplastic</33>. No evidence of <34>mets</34> (nodal or distant). May 2014: presented to <35>SFGH</35> with <36>epigastric</36> and <37>RUQ pain</37>, along with <38>10# weight loss</38>; no known <39>hyperglycemia</39> or <40>hypoglycemia</40>; no <41>diarrhea</41>/<42>flushing</42> <43>CT scan</43> (+) <44>large pancreatic mass</44> (6.4 x 4.8 cm); no <45>liver lesions</45>. <46>Labs</46> from 06/10/14 show <47>ALT</47> and <48>AST</48> of *****/*****, <49>AlkP</49> of 1104, <50>TB</50> of 1.7. <51>Hep B SAg NR</51>, <52>Cr</52> 0.67. 06/29/14: <53>CT</53> at ***** (+) <54>ill-defined pancreatic mass</54> measuring 5.7 x 6 cm-compared to 4.7 x 6.4 cm on 05/17/2014. The <55>mass</55> abuts the <56>portal vein</56> and resides underneath the <57>celiac trunk</57> encasing less than 180 of the <58>celiac trunk</58>. The <59>soft tissue mass</59> encases at least 180 of the <60>superior mesenteric vein</60> and extends to the <61>left anterior pararenal space</61>. The <62>common bile duct</62> is <63>dilated</63>. <64>Cr</64> 0.77 <65>fasting glucose</65> 66 <66>AST</66> 188, <67>ALT</67>
``` 
