<1>alkaline phosphatase</1> 823, <2>total bilirubin</2> 2.9, <3>gamma GT</3> 1527  <4>gastrin level</4> 425 pg per mL [ patient on <5>omeprazole</5>],   <6>pancreatic polypeptide</6> 260 pg per mL [*****-*****],   <7>VIP</7> 45 pg per mL   <8>WBC</8> 6.5, <9>hemoglobin</9> 12.8, <10>platelets</10> 370   <11>C-peptide</11> 1.3 ng per mL, <12>proinsulin</12> 400 pmol per liter  <13>CA 19-9</13> 39 U/mL [<36]   <14>chromogranin A</14> 198 ng per mL [probably not fasting]  <15>glucagon</15> less than 134 pg per mL.   07/22/14: <16>EUS FNA</16>: benign   <17>Mass</17> at least 25 x 25 mm   <18>FBS</18> to 50's, but tolerating regular diet   <19>ERCP</19>(+) <20>bulging ampulla</20>, suggestive of <21>tumor/mass effect</21>. The <22>pancreatic duct</22> demonstrated findings consistent with a <23>large invasive tumor</23> in the <24>head of the pancreas</24>. Despite multiple cannulation attempts, including a <25>precut biliary sphincterotomy</25>, access to the <26>common bile duct</26> could not be achieved, likely due to distortion and possible invasion by the <27>pancreatic mass</27>.   08/04/14: <28>EUS</28> (+) 41mm <29>mass</29> was identified in the <30>head of the pancreas</30>; <31>FNA</31> (+) <32>endocrine tumor</32>; cell count too low for accurate index, 5% *****   Underwent <33>ERCP</33> 08/25/14 with <34>stricture</34> noted in the <35>proximal common bile duct</35> with upstream <36>dilation</36>, <37>sphincterotomy</37> was performed and <38>wire stent</38> was placed
