Most recent imaging was personally reviewed and interpreted in conjunction with formal radiology reports.     <1>CT ABDOMEN/PELVIS WITHOUT CONTRAST</1>  10/14/2016   FINDINGS: Evaluation of the solid organs and vascular structures is limited without intravenous contrast. Visualized lung bases:  <2>Large right pleural effusion</2> and <3>small left pleural effusion</3> with adjacent <4>atelectasis</4>, similar to 10/07/2016. Bones:  No suspicious lesions <5>Liver</5>/<6>Pancreas</6>:  Interval placement of <7>pancreatic duct stent</7> and <8>common bile duct stent</8>. Expected <9>pneumobilia</9> status post stent placement. Known infiltrative <10>pancreatic head and uncinate process mass</10> consistent with <11>adenocarcinoma</11> is better evaluated at prior contrast-enhanced CT 09/08/2016. <12>Gallbladder</12>:  Unremarkable <13>Spleen</13>:  Unremarkable <14>Adrenal Glands</14>:  Unremarkable <15>Kidneys</15>:  <16>Right renal cyst</16>. <17>GI Tract</17>:  Unremarkable. No evidence of <18>bowel obstruction</18>. Vasculature:  Status post <19>aortobiiliac stent graft</19>. <20>Lymphadenopathy</20>: Prominent <21>gastrohepatic lymph nodes</21> and <22>mesenteric lymph nodes</22> better evaluated at contrast-enhanced CT 09/08/2016.
``` 
