Spleen: Unremarkable Pancreas: No significant change in the <1>hypoattenuating necrotic pancreatic mass</1> in the <2>pancreatic body</2> that measures approximately <3>4.0 x 3.2 cm</3> in transaxial dimension. The mass encases and obliterates the <4>proximal celiac artery</4> and partially encases the <5>superior mesenteric artery</5>. The mass partially encases and significantly narrows the <6>superior mesenteric vein</6> and there is complete occlusion of the <7>splenic vein</7>. The <8>main portal vein</8> is patent but significantly narrowed at the ***** confluence. There is a marked amount of <9>venous congestion</9> in the pelvis due to the significant superior mesenteric vein narrowing. There is <10>atrophy of the pancreatic tail</10>. The <11>common bile duct</11> is nondilated. No intrahepatic biliary ductal dilation. Adrenal Glands: Unremarkable Kidneys: <12>Left kidney superior pole simple cyst</12> measuring <13>1.7-cm</13>. GI Tract: Note is made of <14>antral wall thickening</14> which was seen on prior. Pelvis: Unremarkable Lymphadenopathy: Absent Ascites: Absent Bones: No suspicious lesions IMPRESSION: 1. No significant change in size of the <15>pancreatic body and tail necrotic mass</15>. The mass is resulting in severe narrowing of the superior mesenteric vein and obliteration of the splenic vein. The <16>celiac axis</16> is completely encased and obstructed in its proximal portion. //ALERT// 2. New ill-defined low attenuating lesion in <17>segment 6 of the liver</17> is concerning for <18>metastatic disease</18>. 3. There is <19>circumferential gastric antral wall thickening</19> which may be secondary to <20>gastritis</20>. Impression and Recommendations: In summary, Ms. ***** appears to be doing well with her current <21>chemotherapy regimen</21> consisting of an alternating-week schedule of <22>gemcitabine</22> plus <23>capecitabine</23> for her <24>advanced pancreatic cancer</24>. She maintains a good ***** overall and her *****-<25>9 biomarker</25> has been declining. I went over in careful detail the radiographic findings from her recent <26>CT</26> with one of our radiologists, and
``` 
