ner_results: ```plaintext
 unchanged in size and appearance compared to most recent exam on 05/07/2021, though slightly increased in size compared to exam from 11/20/2020. For reference, a right upper lobe <1>nodule</1> measures 4 mm, previously 2.5 mm on 11/20/2020 (series 306, image 96). The left upper lobe <2>nodule</2> measures 6 mm, previously 4 mm on 11/07/2019 (series 306, image 116). No new suspicious <3>nodule</3>.    <4>PLEURA</4>:  No <5>pleural effusion</5> or <6>pneumothorax</6>.    <7>MEDIASTINUM</7>:   No <8>lymphadenopathy</8>.    <9>HEART</9>/***** *****:  Normal <10>heart size</10>. No <11>pericardial effusion</11>. Normal caliber <12>thoracic aorta</12> and <13>main pulmonary artery</13>.    <14>BONES</14>/<15>SOFT TISSUES</15>:  <16>Subacute posterolateral right ninth rib fracture</16> and <17>anterolateral left sixth rib fracture</17>, new since prior exam. Unchanged <18>superior endplate deformities</18> involving the <19>T11 vertebral body</19> and <20>T12 vertebral body</20>.    <21>IMPRESSION</21>:   1.  No new suspicious <22>nodule</22>.  2.  Multiple <23>pulmonary nodules</23>, not significantly changed from most recent comparison on 05/07/2021, though demonstrating slight increase in size compared to more remote exams.  3.  <24>Subacute posterolateral right ninth rib fracture</24> and <25>anterolateral left sixth rib fracture</25>, new since prior exam on 05/07/2021. Correlate with interval history of <26>trauma</26>.
``` 
