Subjective:    This is a very pleasant 50-year-old woman with the aforementioned diagnosis.  *****, her mother was under our care for <1>metastatic pancreatic adenocarcinoma</1>. Her mother had been doing well but suddenly developed <2>sepsis</2> and a <3>bowel perforation</3> and died just prior to her daughter's diagnosis.    The patient's diagnosis was triggered by the symptoms of <4>dyspepsia</4> that were triggered by food.  This started about a month ago.  She's also had a few months of unexplained <5>weight loss</5>, which she thought might be due to stress.  She had also noticed <6>early satiety</6> and had <7>back pain</7> that radiated to her abdomen.  She was also <8>fatigued</8>.    <9>CT scan</9> dated March 03 showed a <10>mass</10> involving the <11>pancreatic head</11> encasing the <12>proximal celiac axis</12> and region of the <13>portal mesenteric confluent</13>.  This was confirmed on <14>EUS</14> on March 16 at which time a <15>fine needle aspirate</15> was done confirming <16>adenocarcinoma</16>.    When we initially saw her, she appeared to have impending <17>biliary duct obstruction</17>.  We referred her for an <18>ERCP</18> and she was also found to have some threat of obstruction in the <19>duodenum</19>. We also repeated her <20>CT scan</20> and this again confirmed <21>locally advanced disease</21>.    We then started treatment with modified *****. She completed <22>12 cycles</22>. She initially did not not tolerate it well. However, we reduced her doses across the board and this helped a lot. She then went on <23>surveillance</23>. During this time, she required placement of a <24>duodenal stent</24>.    We saw her in December, she clearly had progressing disease with new <25>ascites</25>. She also had <26>tumor ingrowth</26> in her <27>duodenal stent</27> requiring placement of a new stent within the stent.    We then started <28>gemcitabine</28> and <29>Abraxane</29>. She's had one full <30>cycle</30>. She is tolerating <31>therapy</31> reasonably well. Her <32>appetite</32> is variable. She's lost <33>14 pounds</33>. She is quite <34>constipated</34> from her <35>narcotics</35> but can get relief with <36>senna</36> and <37>docusate sodium</37>.    Her <38>pain</38> is not optimally controlled.
``` 
