ner_results: ```plaintext
 cm, without measurable disease elsewhere in the chest, abdomen, or pelvis. However, the ultimate decision at ***** ***** ***** was not to pursue a <1>surgical approach</1>, given the extent of his <2>peritoneal disease</2> preoperatively. He was on a <3>chemotherapy holiday</3> for 8 months, with serial imaging showing relatively stable disease but the patient noting some increasing <4>abdominal pain</4> toward the end of 2014. On this basis, he restarted <5>chemotherapy</5> with ***** in October 2014 and received <6>9 cycles</6> in total. Most recent <7>CT scans</7> on 03/03/2015 showed minimal change/slight enlargement in his <8>pancreatic tail mass</8>, extending into the <9>stomach</9>, <10>L kidney</10>, <11>proximal descending colon</11>, and <12>splenic hilum</12>, with <13>splenic vein occlusion</13>/<14>gastric varices</14>; as well as stable <15>sub-cm peritoneal metastases</15>. At the last visit we discussed various options for further treatment, including <16>immunotherapy-based clinical trials</16>. The patient is interested in the possibility of participating in a <17>clinical trial</17> and returns today to discuss this further. He has not received any further <18>chemotherapy</18> in the meantime. Interval history/review of systems - Feeling well overall, no major complaints - Staying active, playing tennis and riding his bike regularly (<19>ECOG PS 0</19>) - Appetite reasonably well-maintained, weight stable - <20>Abdominal pain</20> had initially disappeared when he resumed <21>chemotherapy</21>, although more recently he notes occasional <22>bilateral subcostal discomfort</22>, for which he has just restarted taking <23>hydrocodone</23> within the last week. - Some residual <24>peripheral sensory neuropathy</24> from original *****, unchanged - No <25>fevers</25>/<26>chills</26>, <27>cough</27>, <28>SOB</28>, <29>rash</29>, <30>dysuria</30>, <31>N/V/D</31>. Medications the patient states to be taking prior to today's encounter. Medication Sig  <32>amLODIPine-valsartan (EXFORGE)</32> 10-320 mg tablet Take 1 tablet by mouth Daily.  <33>dexlansoprazole (DEXILANT)</33> 60 mg ***** ***** ***** Take 60 mg by mouth Daily.  <34>LORazepam (ATIVAN)</34> 0.5 mg tablet Take 0.5 mg by mouth every 6 (six) hours as needed for <35>Anxiety</35>.  <36>pilocarpine (ISOPTO *****)</36> 0.5 % ophthalmic solution Place 1-2 drops into both eyes 4 (four) times daily.
