ner_results: ```plaintext
invasive <1>carcinoma</1> identified. 4 <2>lymph nodes</2> were negative. Pt did well until April 2016, when he developed recurrent <3>abdominal pain</3>, for which a repeat <4>CT AP</4> was obtained locally and showed a dilated remnant distal <5>bile duct</5> within the <6>pancreatic head</6>. <7>ERCP/EUS</7> on May 1716 (at *****) showed <8>1.5cm mass</8> in the remnant distal bile duct with <9>high grade dysplasia</9> on <10>biopsy</10> (notably, the <11>pancreas</11> appeared normal). He was scheduled to have ***** in June 2016, but declined <12>surgery</12> in favor of <13>herbal/alternative therapies</13>. He was lost to follow up until November 2019 when he presented with abdominal pain and a <14>CT A/P</14> on 12/14/19 showed an enlarging pancreatic head mass (compared to April 2016) though the official report comments on a normal pancreas. An <15>ERCP/EUS</15> performed locally on 12/27/19 showed an <16>ampullary mass</16>--<17>brushings</17> of the bile duct showed <18>non small cell carcinoma</18> while a biopsy of the ampulla of ***** showed <19>invasive adenocarcinoma</19>. After consultation with Dr. *****, plan was made for a ***** <20>resection</20> on 01/18/20. However, intraoperatively he was found to have a pancreatic head mass with <21>tumor involvement</21> of the <22>proper hepatic artery</22> and <23>portal vein</23>. After consultation with Dr. ***** in the OR, the mass was felt to be unresectable, and the surgery was aborted--rather a ***** <24>end-side hepatojejunostomy</24> was performed. <25>Pathology</25> from biopsy of the pancreas confirmed invasive adenocarcinoma. There was also invasive adenocarcinoma in the bile duct excision. He established care with UCSF <26>GI Med Onc</26> on 03/02/20. 03/07/20: <27>Pancreatic Tumor</27> *****: Reviewed <28>scans</28>, pathology. See 03/02/20 initial consult note for full <29>TB discussion</29>. Overall no consensus about whether <30>ampullary</30>, <31>biliary</31>, or <32>pancreatic</32>. Suggestion to <33>trt</33> with *****/<34>cis</34>/<35>abraxane</35> if tolerated. 03/16/20: Follow up: pt opted for *****/abraxane to trt ***** given c/f <36>toxicity</36> with three drug regimen 03/23/20: <37>C1D1</37> <38>Gemcitabine</38>/<39>Abraxane</39>. <40>1u pRBC</40> for <41>hemoglobin</41>. <42>CA 19-9</42> = <43>28</43> 03/30/20: ***** Gemcitabine/Abraxane 04/06/20: Presented for ***** *****/abraxane. <44>ANC</44> <45>500</45>. Trt held and given ***** x2. Pt subsequently opted to delay trt to April 20 so that he could meet his new grandchild.
``` 
