ner_results: ```plaintext
Subjective:    This is a very pleasant 66-year-old woman who we first saw in early May 2012.  At that time, she was status post <1>pylorus sparing</1> ***** done on 05/04/2012.  Pathology showed a <2>2.5 cm well to moderately differentiated adenocarcinoma</2> with a positive <3>retroperitoneal margin</3> in <4>8 of 12 lymph nodes</4> were also positive.  She was started on adjuvant treatment with fixed dose rate <5>gemcitabine</5> plus <6>capecitabine</6>.  She has completed <7>six 28 day cycles</7>.    She does have known <8>adnexal cystic lesions</8> and is being followed by her gynecologist.  A repeat <9>pelvic ultrasound</9> done in 2918 showed no change. She saw Dr. ***** regarding this. His impression is that this is benign and can also be followed with surveillance.     She also has evidence for <10>aortic stenosis</10> on ***** ***** scan. She has been evaluated for this and there is no current indication for intervention.    In March 2014, she developed severe <11>abdominal pain</11> and was admitted to the hospital for <12>pancreatitis</12>. Attempts at <13>enteroscopy</13> were unsuccessful and her symptoms resolved. In February of this year she also had another episode of <14>acute pancreatitis</14>. This resolved without sequelae. A followup <15>EUS</15> was done on 05/10/2015. This was unremarkable and <16>FNA</16> revealed <17>acute pancreatitis</17>.    She developed a <18>R frozen shoulder</18> and had <19>cortisone injections</19> about 1 year ago. She also had a similar problem in the <20>left shoulder</20> and was treated with <21>physical therapy</21> and repeated <22>cortisone injections</22>.    She's been seeing an endocrinologist because of fluctuating <23>calcium</23> and <24>potassium levels</24>. She was found to be <25>hyperthyroid</25> and she is now being treated with <26>methimazole</26>.    Her husband died at the end of December 2016. This has been very difficult for her but she is coping better now.     In November 2017, she developed an increase in a <27>nodular consolidation</27> in her <28>right lung</28>. This was <29>PET avid</29>. She was referred for a <30>VATS wedge resection</30> and this revealed a <31>mucinous</31>
``` 
