ner_results: ```plaintext
followed by adjuvant therapy with <1>pulmonary recurrence</1> documented in December 2017, currently with no evidence for recurrent disease 2. Recurrent episodes of <2>acute pancreatitis</2>, probably idiopathic 3. <3>Osteoporosis</3> 4. <4>ECOG 0</4> 5. <5>Hyperthyroidism</5>, under treatment 6. <6>Solitary pulmonary metastasis</6>, resected with no current evidence for progressive disease. 7. Unchanged <7>pulmonary nodule</7> of uncertain significance 8. Probable side branch <8>IPMN</8>, stable 9. <9>Hyperglycemia</9> consistent with <10>type 2 diabetes</10> 10. <11>Arteriosclerotic vascular disease</11> Plan: She will continue on surveillance. We'll see her again in 6 months. I performed this consultation using real-time <12>Telehealth</12> tools, including a live video connection between my location and the patient's location. Prior to initiating the consultation, I obtained informed verbal consent to perform this consultation using <13>Telehealth</13> tools and answered all the questions about the <14>Telehealth</14> interaction. I spent a total of 30 minutes in face-to-face time with the patient and in non-face-to-face activities conducted today 07/27/2022 directly related to this video visit, including reviewing records and tests, obtaining history and exam, placing orders, communicating with other healthcare professionals, counseling the patient, family or caregiver, documenting in the medical record, and/or care coordination for the diagnoses above.
