chemotherapy</35>. He denies any <36>cancer related pain</36> but continues to have flares of <37>gouty arthritis</37>. He manages his <38>nausea</38> with frequent <39>Compazine</39>. He is experiencing <40>mild neuropathy</40> and <41>cold sensitivity</41> primarily on his hands. This usually  resolves with in a couple of days after treatment. He has <42>progressive fatigue</42> and naps daily. He is losing some <43>hair</43> on the top of his head. He tends to be <44>anxious</44> at the time of his <45>CT scan</45>.
