 the prior exam. <1>Reticulation</1> and <2>interlobular septal thickening</2> in the lower lobes is more prominent. There is increased <3>subpleural reticulation</3> and <4>groundglass opacity</4> in the lower lobes. There is a new <5>1 cm nodular focus of consolidation</5> in the <6>right upper lobe</6> (series 2, image 124) abutting the fissure.    <7>HEART/MEDIASTINUM/VESSELS</7>:   No <8>thoracic lymphadenopathy</8>. Normal <9>heart size</9>. No <10>pericardial effusion</10>. Normal caliber <11>thoracic aorta</11> and <12>pulmonary artery</12>.    <13>VISIBLE ABDOMEN</13>:  Please see separate <14>abdomen/pelvis CT</14> report of the same date.    <15>BONES/SOFT TISSUES</15>:  No suspicious bone or soft tissue lesions.    <16>IMPRESSION</16>:     1. Increased patchy bilateral <17>groundglass opacities</17> and increased <18>intralobular septal thickening</18>, <19>subpleural</19> and <20>interstitial reticulation</20> in the <21>lung bases</21>. In the absence of <22>infectious symptoms</22>, this is favored to represent sequelae of <23>drug reaction</23>.     2. New <24>1 cm right upper lobe nodule/nodular focus of consolidation</24> which is favored to be part of the above described process. A solitary <25>metastasis</25> is possible but less likely and continued follow-up can be performed to ensure stability/resolution. No other evidence of <26>metastatic disease</26> in the chest.    <27>Impression and Recommendations</27>:  In summary, Mr. ***** is a <28>73 y.o. male</28> s/p ***** resection of a <29>Stage II B (pT3N1) pancreatic adenocarcinoma</29>, followed by <30>adjuvant chemotherapy</30> consisting of the combination of <31>gemcitabine</31> plus *****-<32>paclitaxel</32> per the international randomized phase III ***** trial. He has now completed <33>6 of a planned 6 cycles of treatment</33>, dose reduced x 2 levels due to <34>asymptomatic neutropenia</34>. He developed some mild treatment-related <35>AEs</35> (<36>peripheral sensory neuropathy</36>, <37>fatigue</37> -- both <38>grade 1</38>) that I reassured him should gradually improve off treatment.     Recent <39>CT scans</39> are likewise reassuring for the absence of <40>disease recurrence</40>, including the <41>non-specific pulmonary findings</41> that I explained to him are 
