ner_results: ```plaintext
Current Outpatient Medications Medication Instructions 
 <1>acetaminophen (TYLENOL) 500 mg</1>, <2>Oral</2>, <3>Every 6 Hours PRN</3> 
 <4>albuterol 90 mcg/actuation metered dose inhaler</4> <5>inhale 2 puffs by mouth every 4 hours if needed</5> 
 <6>beclomethasone (QVAR *****) 80 mcg/actuation breath activated inhaler</6> <7>1 puff</7>, <8>Inhalation</8>, <9>Daily PRN</9> 
 <10>cetirizine (ZYRTEC) 10 mg tablet</10> <11>Oral</11> 
 <12>cholecalciferol (vitamin D3) 5,000 Units</12>, <13>Daily Scheduled</13> 
 <14>***** SYRINGE 300 mg/2 mL syringe</14> No dose, route, or frequency recorded. 
 <15>FLUTICASONE PROPIONATE NASAL 93 mcg</15>, <16>Daily PRN</16> 
 <17>HYDROcodone-acetaminophen (NORCO) 5-325 mg tablet</17> <18>1 tablet</18>, <19>Oral</19>, <20>Every 6 Hours PRN</20> 
 <21>HYDROcodone-acetaminophen (NORCO) 5-325 mg tablet</21> <22>1-2 tabs q4-6 hours prn pain</22> 
 <23>naloxone 4 mg/actuation SPRAYNAERO</23> <24>1 spray</24>, <25>Nasal</25>, <26>Once PRN</26>, <27>Call 911</27>. <28>Repeat if needed</28> 
 <29>ondansetron (ZOFRAN) 8 mg tablet</29> <30>Take 1 tab by mouth twice a day for 2 days after each chemo treatment</30>, then <31>take 1 tab three times a day as needed for nausea and vomiting</31>. 
 <32>pantoprazole</32>
``` 
