bifurcation.  - A <1>CA 19-9</1> measured on 01/14/2018 was <2>.   - An <3>ERCP</3> was performed on 01/15/2018, with placement of a <4>metal stent</4> in the <5>distal bile duct</5>, and <6>PD pigtail stent</6>. <7>EUS</7> with <8>FNA</8> of the <9>pancreatic mass</9> revealed <10>adenocarcinoma</10>, with <11>MMR proteins</11> all intact by <12>IHC</12>.     The <13>pt</13> was resuscitated with <14>IVF</14> and discharged on 01/16/18 with follow up. <15>Labs</15> on discharge were notable for a <16>Tbili</16> of <17>5.2</17>. <18>Labs</18> on 01/22/18 showed a normal <19>bilirubin</19> of <20>1.2</20>, along ***** in other <21>LFTs</21>, with an <22>AST</22> of <23>30</23>, <24>ALT</24> <25>124</25>, and <26>alk phos</26> of <27>234</27>.     01/28/18: Initial consultation with Dr. ***** and consented to <28>clinical trial</28> *****#***** ***** (An *****-*****, *****, Phase 1b/2 Clinical Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of <29>CD40 Agonistic Monoclonal Antibody</29> (*****) Administered Together with <30>Gemcitabine</30> and *****-<31>Paclitaxel</31> with or without <32>PD-1 Blocking Antibody</32> (<33>Nivolumab</33>) in ***** with Previously Untreated <34>Metastatic Pancreatic Adenocarcinoma</34>), and has been randomized to the arm containing *****. This includes the combination of <35>gemcitabine</35> plus *****-<36>paclitaxel</36> on a standard three-week-on, one-week-off dosing schedule; and ***** on day 3 of each 28-day cycle.    Treatment was initiated on 02/08/2018.    Interim History :  Patient presents for consideration of ***** today. She continues to experience <37>fatigue</37>, which has not increased recently. She is able to be active 2-3 hours at home before needing a rest. Also continues to have a persistent <38>non-productive cough</38>. Her <39>L-sided flank pain</39> is mostly better but she occasionally experiences mild pain at this site. Denies any <40>fevers</40>, <41>chills</41>, ***** symptoms, <42>UTI symptoms</42>.     <43>ECOG PS</43> = 1<44>Medications</44> the patient states to be taking prior to today's encounter.   <45>Medication</45> Sig    <46>ascorbic acid</46>, <47>vitamin C</47>, (<48>VITAMIN C</48>) <49>250 mg tablet</49> Take <50>250 mg</50> by mouth Daily.    <51>atorvastatin</51> (<52>LIPITOR</52>) <53>10 mg tablet</53> <54>5 mg</54> Daily.     <55>CALCIUM ORAL</55> Take by mouth.
