SUBJECTIVE  This is a very pleasant 87-year-old gentleman with a prior history of <1>bladder cancer</1> that incidentally was associated with a episode of <2>pancreatitis</2>. He was on surveillance for his <3>bladder cancer</3> when a <4>mass in the tail of the pancreas</4> was identified. Follow-up scan showed that the <5>mass</5> was progressing and on June 17, an <6>EUS directed biopsy</6> revealed <7>adenocarcinoma</7>.    He was referred to us at that point. However, as his <8>disease</8> appeared to be resectable, we immediately referred him to Dr.***** who did a <9>laparoscopic distal pancreatectomy</9>. Because of <10>renal and splenic invasion</10>, the <11>left kidney</11> and <12>left adrenal</12> and <13>spleen</13> were included in the resection. Margins were negative and <14>23 lymph nodes</14> were negative. Tissue was <15>MMR intact</15>.    We recommended <16>adjuvant therapy</16> with <17>gemcitabine</17> and <18>capecitabine</18>. He has had <19>6 cycles</19> and is on surveillance.     He is doing well. Energy level is good. Weight is stable. Appetite is good. No pain currently. Regular bowel movements. Slow urine stream secondary to <20>enlarged prostate</20>.    He had an episode of <21>chest pain</21> last Tues and called 911. Work up was unremarkable.    He has a history of <22>bladder cancer</22> his last surveillance <23>cystoscopy</23> was unremarkable.    <24>Germline testing</24> revealed an increased risk allele identified as <25>SPINK1 c.101A>G</25>    PAST MEDICAL HISTORY:    MEDICAL ILLNESSES:  History of <26>bladder cancer</26> requiring resection  <27>aortic valvular disease</27> requiring replacement  <28>pacemaker</28> for rate control  <29>BPH</29>      PRIOR SURGERIES:  <30>Robotic diverticulum cystectomy</30>, <31>bladder</31>, July 2017  <32>aortic valve replacement</32>, October 2017    INJURIES:  None reported    CURRENT MEDICATIONS:  No outpatient medications have been marked as taking for the 09/16/20 encounter (Appointment) with ***** ***** *****, MD.       ALLERGIES:  Allergies/Contraindications   Allergen Reactions    <33>Terbinafine Hcl</33>      <34>Loss sense of taste</34> (<35>LAMISIL</35>)     <36>Tamsulosin</36> Other (See Comments)     <37>Nasal drainage</37> and <38>eyes</38> 
