day 8, he developed <1>rigors</1> and <2>fever</2> to 102 and was briefly hospitalized at ***** in ***** *****. No pathogens were identified and he was discharged on <3>Augmentin</3>. Because of this hospitalization, day 15 of <4>cycle 1</4> was held. His second <5>cycle</5> was complicated by the development of progressive <6>fatigue</6> and <7>weakness</7>. She now needs a <8>walker</8> to ambulate and a <9>bedside commode</9>. He is also developed generalized <10>edema</10> and <11>peeling of his skin</11> as well as <12>mouth sores</12> which are responding to ***** <13>mouthwash</13>. He also experienced <14>fever</14> to 101.9 and was again hospitalized on <15>July 08</15>. During that ***** <16>infection</16> was identified. A repeat <17>CT scan</17> showed an improvement in the size of the <18>pancreas</18> as well as diminished <19>adenopathy</19>. However, more <20>ascites</20> was described. On the positive side, he is not having any <21>pain</21>. He is experiencing <22>bladder urgency</22> and <23>bowel urgency</23> and has some <24>incontinence</24>. His <25>appetite</25> is poor. He has a history of <26>asthma</26> and felt that he was having problems from mount. He self started <27>prednisone</27> 2 days ago. PAST MEDICAL HISTORY: MEDICAL ILLNESSES: <28>Asthma</28>, since 1990, controlled <29>BPH</29>, controlled <30>hypertension</30> for the last 5 years history of <31>melanoma</31> x4, right lateral ankle, back, head, arm, all resected PRIOR SURGERIES: <32>Total hip</32>, 2017 <33>knee replacement</33>, 2011 <34>rotator cuff surgery</34> bilaterally <35>inguinal hernia repair</35>, 2017 INJURIES: No major injuries described
