treatment. As allowed per study protocol, he was crossed over to the experimental <1>immunotherapy</1> arm consisting of the combination of q2 weekly <2>atezolizumab</2>, a <3>PD-L1 inhibitor</3>, together with <4>cobimetinib</4>, an oral <5>MEK inhibitor</5>. Screening over the next month included <6>Ophthalmology exam</6>, <7>echocardiogram</7>, and <8>tumor biopsy</8> (<9>liver</9>), all performed before the ***** holidays.  - 02/06/2018: <10>Cycle 1 day 1 of study treatment</10>    The patient is now in the midst of <11>cycle #2</11> (<12>atezolizumab</12> on days 1 and 15 and <13>cobimetinib</13> daily x 21 of 28 days), with which he remains fully compliant and is tolerating treatment well.    On present review of systems, Mr. ***** notes:  - A couple of transient <14>dizzy spells</14> last week during rest (<15>10 minutes</15> apiece)  - No associated <16>chest pressure</16> or <17>SOB</17>  - Prior (mild) <18>rash</18> in <19>nasolabial folds</19> and ***** has essentially dissipated with use of <20>Aquaphor</20>  - Previously described intermittent <21>RUQ/back discomfort</21> has mostly subsided; not requiring any <22>analgesics</22>  - Regular <23>BMs</23> (multiple per day); mostly well-formed but sometimes loose (no frank <24>diarrhea</24>)  - <25>Appetite</25> generally well-maintained  - No recent <26>night sweats</26>  - Waxing/waxing slight <27>LE edema</27>  - <28>Peripheral sensory neuropathy</28> from prior <29>chemotherapy</29> slightly improving  - Staying generally active; <30>ECOG PS 0</30>        Medications the patient states to be taking prior to today's encounter.   Medication Sig    <31>acyclovir</31> (<32>ZOVIRAX</32>) <33>400 mg tablet</33>     <34>pantoprazole</34> (<35>PROTONIX</35>) <36>40 mg EC tablet</36> Take <37>40 mg</37> by mouth.         Allergies/Contraindications  <38>No Known Allergies</38>      Comprehensive past medical, family, and social history which was performed during a previous encounter was re-examined and reviewed with the patient. There is nothing new to add at today's visit. For details, please refer to my original consultation note in this chart.      Physical Exam:    <39>Blood pressure</39> *****/*****, <40>pulse</40> <41>55</41>, <42>temperature</42> <43>36.6 C</43> (<44>97.8 F</44>), temperature source <45>Oral</45>, <46>resp. rate</46> <47>16</47>,
