Ms. ***** is a 61 y.o. female who returns to our GI Oncology practice at the UCSF Comprehensive Cancer Center for follow-up of her advanced <1>intrahepatic cholangiocarcinoma</1> (as well as a concurrent indolent, non-progressive <2>non-functional PNET</2>). She previously received <3>gemcitabine</3>/<4>cisplatin</4> and ***** back in 2013-14, and more recently was enrolled on a <5>phase II trial</5> of <6>GM-CSF</6>/<7>pembrolizumab</7> specific for <8>biliary tract cancers</8>. However, she had to be taken off study last month due to gradual, albeit relatively asymptomatic, <9>disease progression</9>, following <10>7 treatment cycles</10> in total. We talked about restarting <11>chemotherapy</11> at her last visit before the ***** holidays but she wished to take some time to decide how she wished to proceed.    Interval history/review of systems  Due to evidence of some third-spacing, with <12>ascites</12> and a <13>R-sided pleural effusion</13>, she underwent both <14>paracentesis</14> (3400 cc) and <15>R-sided thoracentesis</15> (1000 cc) on <16>06/27/2016</16>. <17>Cytology</17> from both of these fluid samples were benign.     She is increasingly <18>fatigued</18> and far less active than previously. She denies any frank pain. She has developed some <19>jaundice symptoms</19>, with ***** and generalized <20>pruritis</20>. She may have had some transient relief from the perspective of her <21>breathing/cough</21> and <22>abdominal distention</22> post-procedure, but these symptoms have since recurred. She tried <23>Lasix</23> for one week, but self-d/c'ed this b/c it caused some <24>diarrhea</24> (since subsided). <25>Appetite</25> is sluggish. She denies any <26>fevers/chills</26>.      Medications the patient states to be taking prior to today's encounter.   Medication Sig    <27>anastrozole (ARIMIDEX)</27> 1 mg tablet TAKE 1 TABLET EVERY DAY    <28>BYSTOLIC</28> 10 mg tablet TAKE 1 TABLET ORALLY EVERY DAY    <29>calcium carbonate (TUMS)</29> 200 mg calcium (500 mg) chewable tablet Take 1 tablet by mouth once as needed for <30>Heartburn</30>.    <31>fluticasone (FLONASE)</31> 50 mcg/actuation nasal spray 2 sprays by Nasal route Daily.    <32>furosemide</32>
