tube suction, <1>IV hydration</1>, and <2>analgesia</2>. On present review of systems, the patient notes: 
- Some <3>chronic diarrhea</3> up to 5x/day (uses <4>pancreatic enzymes</4> with most meals) 
- <5>Generalized fatigue</5>, slowly improving; trying to stay active and exercise, and still working 
- Healthy appetite; trying to gain weight (<6>50 lb weight loss</6> in total) 
- Some residual <7>peripheral sensory neuropathy</7> (feet mostly) from prior <8>chemotherapy</8> 
- No residual <9>abdominal pain</9> 
- No <10>fevers</10>/<11>chills</11> 
- No <12>SOB</12>/<13>respiratory symptoms</13> 
The remainder of the patient's review of systems was negative. 
Medications the patient states to be taking prior to today's encounter. 
Medication Sig 
<14>acetaminophen (TYLENOL) 500 mg tablet</14> Take 500 mg by mouth every 6 (six) hours as needed. 
<15>lipase-protease-amylase (*****) 24,000-76,000 -120,000 unit CAPDREC capsule</15> Take 1 capsule by mouth 3 (three) times daily with meals. 
No Known <16>Allergies</16> 
Past medical history is fairly unremarkable except for some <17>chronic hearing loss</17>. Childhood surgeries (<18>tonsillectomy</18>, <19>hip repair</19>). 
Personal and social history: Married; works as realtor (owns own business). No tobacco use/social <20>EtOH</20> in the past. 
Physical Exam: 
<21>Blood pressure</21> *****/*****, <22>pulse</22> 52, <23>temperature</23> 35.9 C (96.6 F), temperature source Oral, <24>resp. rate</24> 18, <25>height</25> 188 cm (6' 2.02"), <26>weight</26> 72.122 kg (159 lb), <27>SpO2</27> 99.00%. 
General appearance: No acute distress, conversant, appropriately interactive. Non-toxic, well-appearing. 
Eyes: <28>anicteric sclerae</28>, <29>moist conjunctivae</29>; no lid lag. 
HEENT: Atraumatic; <30>oropharynx clear</30> with <31>moist mucous membranes</31> and no mucosal ulcerations; normal hard and soft palate 
Neck: Full range of motion, supple, no <32>lymphadenopathy</32> 
Lungs/respiratory: <33>Clear to auscultation</33>, with normal respiratory effort and no intercostal retractions 
Cardiovascular: <34>RRR</34>, normal <35>S1 S2</35>, no <36>murmurs</36>, <37>gallops</37>, or <38>rubs</38>. 
Abdomen/GI: <39>Soft</39>, <40>non-tender</40>, <41>nondistended</41>; no <42>masses</42>.
