ner_results: ```plaintext
 of contact with the portal vein and mild focal contact with the superior mesenteric vein, and no arterial encasement.  A <1>CT Chest</1> did not show evidence of intrathoracic metastatic disease.  On 04/07/18 he underwent an <2>EUS</2> and <3>ERCP</3> with Dr. *****.  The <4>EUS</4> showed a 2.9 x 2.5 cm <5>mass in the head of the pancreas</5> that involves the <6>pancreatic duct</6> and <7>bile duct</7> and appeared to involve the <8>splenoportal confluence</8>. Tissue was obtained for <9>cytology</9>.  <10>ERCP</10> showed <11>intrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation</11> with a <12>stricture of the common bile duct</12>. A <13>metallic stent</13> was deployed within the <14>common bile duct</14>.  Ultimately the <15>cytology</15> returned as positive for <16>pancreatic adenocarcinoma</16>, <17>MSS</17>.  The day following his <18>biopsy</18> he developed <19>severe abdominal pain</19> so on 04/08/18 he presented to an <20>OSH ED</20>. His <21>lab tests</21> revealed a mildly elevated <22>lipase</22> but no other significant abnormalities.  No imaging was performed.    Of note is his family history of <23>malignancy</23>.  His mother was diagnosed with <24>pancreatic cancer</24> at age 64, died 65.  Father diagnosed with <25>colon cancer</25> at 70.  His Maternal Grandmother had <26>colon cancer</26>.  Paternal aunt with <27>breast cancer</27>, died at age 37, and his paternal grandfather had <28>stomach cancer</28>.  He has had <29>germ line testing</29> and this was positive for <30>pathogenic APC mutation</30>.    We initially saw him in April 2018 and recommended therapy with <31>gemcitabine</31> and <32>Abraxane</32>. He experienced a delay in starting treatment because of <33>tumor ingrowth into his stent</33> which required <34>revision</34>. He also presented for his day 8 of his first cycle with <35>severe hypertension</35> and a <36>creatinine</36> of 3.59. These problems eventually were controlled and he has completed 6 cycles of therapy. His last 2 cycles were given with alternate week schedule using <37>fixed dose rate gemcitabine</37>.    He was taken to <38>surgery</38> on 11/27/2018. He underwent a <39>portal vein resection</39>. <40>Path report</40> did show <41>residual adenocarcinoma</41>, <42>moderately differentiated</42>, with 8 of 23 <43>lymph</43>
``` 
