ner_results: ```plaintext
 and negative margins.    <1>Imaging</1> since then have shown no recurrent <2>disease</2> in the <3>liver</3>, but slowly growing sub-cm <4>pulmonary nodules</4> (right upper lobe (6 x 6 mm), right lower lobe (8 x 10 mm)). She was seen by Dr. ***** ***** of our Thoracic Surgical faculty practice who took her for <5>robotic right thoracoscopic-assisted right upper lobe apical segment wedge resection</5> (0.6 cm) and <6>right lower lobe lateral/inferior basilar segment wedge resection</6> (0.1 cm) on <7>06/23/2018</7>; both of these specimens were c/w <8>metastatic adenocarcinoma</8>, with negative margins. Postoperatively, she did have a sizeable <9>R pleural effusion</9> requiring <10>thoracentesis</10> x 2 (benign cytology) that gradually resolved on its own.     After her operation, we opted for a period of time vigilant surveillance without immediate resumption of <11>systemic therapy</11>. However, her <12>*****-9 levels</12> gradually ***** upwards, with a <13>CT scan</13> performed here at ***** on <14>12/10/2018</14> showing growing tiny <15>pulmonary nodules</15> (sub-cm) as well as a slightly enlarging 1.3 cm <16>hypodense liver lesion</16>. On these bases, she resumed <17>chemotherapy</17> with the combination of <18>gemcitabine</18> plus *****-<19>paclitaxel</19> starting <20>01/06/2019</20>, on a planned ***** dosing schedule (days 1 and 15 of a 28-day cycle) with ***** <21>prophylaxis</21>. She continued treatment, aside from a 3-week treatment interruption early on for a ***** European cruise, through late May/early June, and was then taken back to the <22>O.R</22> at ***** ***** on <23>07/07/2019</23> for <24>wedge resection of her liver segment VIII metastasis</24> (1.3 cm <25>moderately differentiated adenocarcinoma</25> with negative margins). She made a very smooth postoperative recovery, and ultimately resumed <26>chemotherapy</26> with the same regimen as of <27>08/25/2019</27>.    Interval history/review of systems  Tolerating treatment without difficulty; energy level holding up well, with minimal cumulative <28>peripheral sensory neuropathy</28>. Appetite well-maintained, with only transient post-infusion <29>nausea</29>. Denies any intercurrent <30>fevers</30>, <31>chills</31>, or signs/symptoms of <32>infection</32>. No localizing pain aside from slight <33>abdominal discomfort</33> on occasion that is relieved with <34>BMs</34>. No <35>SOB</35>, <36>cough</36>, or <37>respiratory symptoms</37>.    The remainder of a full review of systems is negative.
``` 
