 11/05/2020     <1>Lab Results</1>   <2>Component</2> <3>Value</3> <4>Date</4>    <5>Cancer Antigen 19-9</5> <6>456</6> (H) 11/21/2020    <7>Cancer Antigen 19-9</7> <8>318</8> (H) 11/07/2020    <9>Cancer Antigen 19-9</9> <10>282</10> (H) 10/03/2020         Most recent <11>imaging</11> was personally reviewed and interpreted in conjunction with formal <12>radiology reports</12>, as follows:     <13>Result Date</13>: 12/05/2020  <14>CT-PET SCAN</14>  Formal report pending; per my review and discussion with <15>Radiology</15>, key finding = a new <16>hypodense liver lesion</16> in <17>R hepatic lobe</17> with surrounding <18>hyperemia</18>. I do not appreciate other new sites of progression, although will await final read.      <19>Result Date</19>: 10/16/2020  <20>CT CHEST PULMONARY EMBOLISM (CTPE)</20>   <21>FINDINGS</21>: <22>PULMONARY ARTERIES</22>: No <23>pulmonary embolism</23> through the <24>subsegmental pulmonary arteries</24>. <25>LUNGS</25>: <26>Significant severe cystic bronchiectasis</26> involving the <27>left upper lobe</27>, <28>lingular</28>, <29>right upper lobe</29>, <30>middle lobe</30> and <31>lower lobe</31>. <32>Interval development of new groundglass opacity</32> in the <33>right lower lobe</33> and <34>consolidation</34> in the <35>left lower lobe</35> with additional <36>nodular foci of consolidation</36> in the <37>right lower lobe</37>. <38>PLEURA</38>: No evidence of <39>pleural effusion</39> <40>MEDIASTINUM</40>: Unchanged <41>mediastinal and bilateral hilar lymphadenopathy</41> <42>HEART</42>/***** *****: Normal <43>cardiac size</43>. <44>Chest port</44> terminates near the <45>cavoatrial junction</45> <46>BONES/SOFT TISSUES</46>: No suspicious <47>osseous lesions</47>     1.  No evidence of <48>pulmonary embolus</48> 2.  <49>Significant severe cystic bronchiectasis</49> involving the <50>left upper lobe</50>, <51>lingular</51>, <52>right upper lobe</52>, <53>middle lobe</53> and <54>lower lobe</54>, findings compatible with known history of <55>cystic fibrosis</55>. 3.  <56>Interval development of scattered groundglass opacity</56> in the <57>right lower lobe</57> which might represent foci of <58>infection</58> or <59>hemorrhage</59> and new <60>consolidation</60> in the <61>left lower lobe</61> with scattered foci of <62>nodular consolidation</62> in the <63>right lower lobe</63> concerning for <64>pneumonia</64> and/or <65>hemorrhage</65>.    <66>Impression and Recommendations</66>:  In summary, Ms. ***** is a 39 y.o. female with <67>pancreatic cancer</67>
