6>surveillance imaging</46> showed growth in involved <47>lymph nodes</47>. Because his course has been unusually indolent, we elected to <48>biopsy</48> one of the nodes to be sure we understood what we were treating. <49>Biopsy</49> showed <50>adenocarcinoma</50>. He has resumed <51>treatment</51>. He is being treated with <52>gemcitabine</52> and <53>Abraxane</53>. He has completed <54>8 cycles of therapy</54> although
