ner_results: ```plaintext
 recommended.    <1>CT abdomen with pancreatic protocol</1> was obtained on 11/25/15 showed the <2>pancreatic head mass</2> with abutment of the <3>superior mesenteric vein</3> with less than 90 degrees contact and probable preserved fat plane between the mass and vein. There was no contact with the <4>SMA</4>. There was additional <5>2.4 x 1.5 cm hypodense structure</5> medial to the mass may represent a <6>metastatic lymph node</6> versus medial extension of the mass and abutment of the <7>proximal right renal artery</7>, with a preserved fat plane. There were additional <8>prominent periportal nodes</8> measuring up to <9>14 x 11 mm</9> which were nonspecific. An <10>enhancing lesion</10> at the <11>lateral interpolar region of the right kidney</11> measuring <12>2.0 x 1.8 cm</12>, suspicious for <13>renal cell carcinoma</13> was also noted.    She was evaluated by Dr. ***** who recommended <14>neoadjuvant chemotherapy</14>. She had <15>ERCP</15> with <16>biliary stent placement</16> on December 02.     *****/*****- *****/*****/*****: Admitted for <17>fever</17> with concern for potential <18>cholangitis</18>. <19>ERCP</19> wasn't performed.    *****/*****- *****/*****/*****: Admitted with <20>cholangitis</20>.  12/27/15: <21>ERCP</21> performed with <22>purulent drainage</22> noted for which <23>small sphincterotomy</23> was performed. Two <24>double pigtail stents</24> were placed in the <25>bilateral ductal systems</25> with good drainage. Discharged with <26>14 days of antibiotics</26> (<27>ciprofloxacin</27> and <28>metronidazole</28>) with a repeat <29>ERCP</29> recommended in 4 weeks.     01/14/16: <30>C1D1</30> ***** (holding <31>irinotecan</31> due to <32>hyperbilirubinemia</32>)    01/24/16: <33>ERCP</33> revealed <34>suppurative cholangitis</34>, replaced one <35>plastic biliary stent</35> and admitted for <36>antibiotics</36> given the <37>cholangitis</37>. Noted a large area of <38>duodenum ulcerated</38> just distal to the bulb concerning for <39>malignant invasion</39>    01/28/16: <40>ERCP</40> when <41>2nd stent</41> placed     02/03/16: <42>ERCP</42> revealed <43>duodenal narrowing</43> due to <44>tumor infiltration</44>. Previously placed <45>plastic stents</45> were removed.  <46>High grade distal CBD stricture</46> seen on <47>cholangiogram</47>. A <48>10 mm x 6 cm Evolution uncovered metal biliary stent</48> was placed with good drainage. 
``` 
