*****/*****-*****/*****/*****: Directly admitted from clinic for worsening <1>ascites</1>, <2>BLE edema</2> and <3>weakness</3>. <4>Paracentesis</4> performed and revealed ***** <5>1.7</5> suggesting <6>portal hypertension</6>. Cytology showed three large, atypical cells which were morphologically similar to the patient's <7>tumor</7>.    10/17/16: <8>CT abd/pelv</8> - Stable moderate intraperitoneal <9>ascites</9> with areas of <10>peritoneal enhancement</10> of the pelvis. Slightly increased <11>omental stranding</11> in the left upper and lower quadrants as well as increased infiltrative retroperitoneal soft tissue in the <12>portocaval region</12>; suspicious for <13>peritoneal carcinomatosis</13>. <14>CA 19-9</14> increased to <15>1008</15>.     10/20/16: <16>C1D1</16> of <17>gemcitabine</17> + <18>capecitabine</18>    10/28/16: ***** delayed due to <19>cytopenias</19> (given on 11/03/16)    11/06/16: <20>Paracentesis</20>    11/10/16: ***** of <21>gemcitabine</21> + <22>capecitabine</22>     *****/*****-*****/*****/*****: Admitted for <23>constipation</23> (no <24>bowel obstruction</24>) and discharged with a <25>bowel regimen</25>; had <26>paracentesis</26> on (<27>1.7L</27> removed). <28>Capecitabine</28> was held during this admission.    Interim History  Since discharge from the hospital, she has not been sleeping well at night but takes naps twice a day. She is up from 1-4 am. She is on <29>methadone</29> and she feels groggy with it. She continues to have lower <30>abdominal pain</30>. Her appetite is lower. She tries to take in <31>protein drink</31>. She will be seen in ***** clinic after he visit with me. Her <32>BM</32> are soft and frequent.
