ner_results: ```plaintext
Subjective:    This is a very pleasant 79-year-old woman from ***** ***** presented with <1>nausea</1> in July and progressed to <2>abdominal pain</2>. She saw her <3>PCP</3> who ordered a routine <4>CT scan of the abdomen</4>. This showed small or dense lesions in the head of the <5>pancreas</5> and some prominence of the <6>pancreatic duct</6>. She was then referred to ***** ***** who performed an <7>EUS</7> and a <8>fine-needle aspiration</8> which confirmed <9>adenocarcinoma</9>. The <10>EUS interpretation</10> suggested that she had <11>SMA encasement</11>. The <12>biopsy</12> recovered a diagnosis of <13>adenocarcinoma</13>.  .  When we initially saw her in consultation, we were concerned that she might have <14>metastatic disease</14>. We did repeat a <15>pancreas protocol CT scan</15> and this confirmed a diagnosis of <16>locally advanced disease</16>. We started her on an alternate week fixed dose rate <17>gemcitabine</17> with <18>capecitabine</18>. She is now received two <19>cycles</19>. She initially had difficulty with <20>skin tenderness on her fingertips</20> and with <21>blisters on her lips</21> which were thought to be related to <22>herpes simplex</22>. She has been treated with <23>acyclovir</23>. However between the <24>lip blisters</24> and <25>tenderness in her fingertips</25>, she received incomplete dosing with <26>capecitabine</26> during her first <27>cycle</27>. Her second <28>cycle</28>, we reduced her <29>capecitabine dose</29> by 20%.     Despite this, she was still unable to complete her <30>capecitabine</30> during the third <31>cycle</31> and it was held on day 16.     Currently, her <32>abdominal pain</32> is well-controlled on <33>Norco</33>. She complains of a <34>low energy level</34> and <35>feeling cold all the time</35>. She still has some <36>peeling on her fingertips</36> especially in the flexor areas. She has some mild <37>nausea</37> which responds to <38>Zofran</38>. She has a good appetite. She has one to 2 soft formed <39>bowel movements</39> daily.    Since we last saw her, a <40>port</40> was placed.    Medications the patient states to be taking prior to today's encounter.   Medication Sig    <41>coenzyme Q10</41> 100 mg capsule Take 300 mg by mouth Daily.    <42>HYDROcodone-acetaminophen (NORCO) 5-325</42>
``` 
